§ `Scenario cases -- Penal Code 1871 agent screen`

§§ `Blank nested records`

`adult Alice` MEANS Actor WITH
    `name` IS "Alice"
    `age in years` IS 30
    `is a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore` IS TRUE
    `is a public servant` IS FALSE
    `is acting or purporting to act in the course of employment` IS FALSE
    `has sufficient maturity of understanding` IS TRUE
    `is of unsound mind at the time of the act` IS FALSE
    `by reason of unsoundness of mind is incapable of knowing the nature of the act` IS FALSE
    `by reason of unsoundness of mind is incapable of knowing the act is wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `by reason of unsoundness of mind is incapable of knowing the act is wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `by reason of unsoundness of mind is completely deprived of any power to control his actions` IS FALSE

`child of 8` MEANS Actor WITH
    `name` IS "Child"
    `age in years` IS 8
    `is a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore` IS TRUE
    `is a public servant` IS FALSE
    `is acting or purporting to act in the course of employment` IS FALSE
    `has sufficient maturity of understanding` IS FALSE
    `is of unsound mind at the time of the act` IS FALSE
    `by reason of unsoundness of mind is incapable of knowing the nature of the act` IS FALSE
    `by reason of unsoundness of mind is incapable of knowing the act is wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `by reason of unsoundness of mind is incapable of knowing the act is wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `by reason of unsoundness of mind is completely deprived of any power to control his actions` IS FALSE

`blank personal information` MEANS `Personal Information Dealing` WITH
    `the information is personal information about an individual` IS FALSE
    `the actor knows or has reason to believe it was obtained without that individual consent` IS FALSE
    `obtains or retains the personal information` IS FALSE
    `supplies offers transmits or makes available the personal information` IS FALSE
    `purpose is use in committing or facilitating an offence` IS FALSE
    `purpose is supply for use in committing or facilitating an offence` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe it will be or is likely to be used to commit or facilitate an offence` IS FALSE
    `merely provides or operates network access or routing facilities` IS FALSE

`blank services` MEANS `Services Obtained` WITH
    `obtains services for self or another` IS FALSE
    `the services are made available on the basis that payment has been is being or will be made` IS FALSE
    `obtains the services without payment or without payment in full` IS FALSE
    `when obtaining knows they are or might be made available on that payment basis` IS FALSE
    `when obtaining intends that payment will not be made or will not be made in full` IS FALSE

`blank fraud` MEANS `Fraud Conduct` WITH
    `makes a false representation` IS FALSE
    `fails to disclose information which the actor is under a legal duty to disclose` IS FALSE
    `abuses a position expected to safeguard the financial interests of another` IS FALSE
    `the representation is untrue or misleading` IS FALSE
    `the actor knows it is or might be untrue or misleading` IS FALSE
    `the representation is submitted to a system or device designed to receive communications` IS FALSE
    `is directly connected with a written or oral contract for the supply of goods or services` IS FALSE
    `the acts were material` IS FALSE

`blank property taking` MEANS `Property Taking` WITH
    `the property is movable` IS FALSE
    `intends to take the property out of the possession of any person` IS FALSE
    `without that person consent` IS FALSE
    `moves the property in order to such taking` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use` IS FALSE
    `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a clerk or servant or employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing death hurt or restraint or fear of death hurt or restraint to any person in order to commit the theft or to effect escape after it or to retain property taken by it` IS FALSE
    `knows that the property was in the possession of a deceased person at the time of that person decease and has not since been in the possession of any person legally entitled to it` IS FALSE

`blank trust` MEANS Trust WITH
    `is entrusted with property or with any dominion over property` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts that property to own use` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly uses or disposes of that property in violation of a direction of law or legal contract touching the trust` IS FALSE
    `intentionally suffers any other person to do so` IS FALSE
    `the entrustment was of property for the purpose of transportation or storage for hire` IS FALSE
    `the accused is an employee or engaged in a capacity with the same fundamental qualities as an employee and was entrusted in that capacity` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in his capacity as a public servant` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in the way of his trade profession or business as a banker merchant factor broker attorney or agent` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in his professional capacity otherwise than by way of such a trade profession or business` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in his capacity as a director of a corporation an officer of an unincorporated association a partner in a partnership a key executive or a fiduciary` IS FALSE

`blank document making` MEANS `Document Making` WITH
    `makes a document or electronic record or part of one` IS FALSE
    `makes signs seals executes or affixes an electronic signature` IS FALSE
    `intends it to be believed that it was made signed sealed executed or affixed by or by the authority of a person by whom the actor knows it was not` IS FALSE
    `without lawful authority alters a document or electronic record in any material part` IS FALSE
    `causes a person who does not know the contents to sign seal execute or alter` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person` IS FALSE
    `intent to support any claim or title` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause any person to part with property` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause any person to enter into any express or implied contract` IS FALSE
    `intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed` IS FALSE

`blank forged document` MEANS `Forged Document` WITH
    `the document or electronic record purports to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice or a register of birth baptism marriage or burial or a register kept by a public servant as such or a certificate document or electronic record purporting to be made by a public servant in his official capacity or an authority to institute or defend a suit or to take any proceedings in it or to confess judgment or a power of attorney` IS FALSE
    `the document purports to be a valuable security or a will or an authority to adopt a child or purports to give authority to any person to make or transfer any valuable security or to receive the principal interest or dividends on it or to receive or deliver any money movable property or valuable security or purports to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money or the delivery of any movable property or valuable security` IS FALSE
    `intends that the document or electronic record forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating` IS FALSE
    `intends that the document or electronic record forged shall harm the reputation of any person or knows that it is likely to be used for that purpose` IS FALSE
    `the document or electronic record is a false document or false electronic record made wholly or in part by forgery` IS FALSE
    `uses as genuine a document or electronic record` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe the document or electronic record to be a forged document or forged electronic record` IS FALSE
    `has in his possession a document or electronic record knowing it to be forged` IS FALSE
    `intends that the document or electronic record shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine` IS FALSE
    `makes or counterfeits any seal plate or other instrument for making an impression` IS FALSE
    `has in his possession any such seal plate or other instrument knowing it to be counterfeit` IS FALSE
    `intends that the seal plate or instrument shall be used for the purpose of committing a forgery which would be punishable under section 467` IS FALSE
    `intends that the seal plate or instrument shall be used for the purpose of committing a forgery which would be punishable under a section of Chapter 18 other than section 467` IS FALSE
    `makes or has in his custody or under his control a machine or implement or paper or other material` IS FALSE
    `to his knowledge the machine implement paper or material is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any false instrument` IS FALSE
    `the machine implement paper or material is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any instrument` IS FALSE
    `intends that he or another person makes a false instrument using the machine implement paper or material in order to induce another person to accept it as genuine or to induce a machine to respond to it as if it were a genuine instrument` IS FALSE
    `intends that by reason of so accepting it the person induced does or does not do some act` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in a person permanently or temporarily losing property including by not getting what he might get` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in a person being deprived of an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in a person being deprived of an opportunity to gain a financial advantage otherwise than by way of remuneration` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in somebody being given an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration from a person` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in somebody being given an opportunity to gain a financial advantage from a person otherwise than by way of remuneration` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will be the result of a person having accepted a false instrument as genuine in connection with his performance of any duty` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced is one induced by a machine responding to the instrument as if it were genuine` IS FALSE
    `the act intended to be induced is one the person has an enforceable duty to do or the omission intended to be induced is of an act the person is not entitled to do` IS FALSE
    `counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating a document or electronic record` IS FALSE
    `has in his possession any material upon or in the substance of which any such device or mark has been counterfeited` IS FALSE
    `intends that the device or mark shall be used for the purpose of giving the appearance of authenticity to any document or electronic record then forged or thereafter to be forged on that material` IS FALSE
    `the device or mark is used for the purpose of authenticating a document described in section 467` IS FALSE
    `cancels destroys or defaces or attempts to cancel destroy or deface or secretes or attempts to secrete a document or commits mischief in respect of it` IS FALSE
    `the document is or purports to be a will or an authority to adopt a child or any valuable security` IS FALSE
    `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person` IS FALSE
    `is a clerk officer or servant or is employed or acting in the capacity of a clerk officer or servant` IS FALSE
    `intentionally and with intent to defraud destroys alters conceals mutilates or falsifies any book electronic record paper writing valuable security or account or a set of them which belongs to or is in the possession of his employer or has been received by him for or on behalf of his employer` IS FALSE
    `intentionally and with intent to defraud makes or abets the making of any false entry in or omits or alters or abets the omission or alteration of any material particular from or in any such book electronic record paper writing valuable security or account or set of them` IS FALSE

`blank currency` MEANS Currency WITH
    `the thing is a bank note being a promissory note or engagement for the payment of money to bearer on demand issued by a person carrying on the business of banking in any part of the world or issued by or under the authority of the government of any country or territory and intended to be used as equivalent to or as a substitute for money` IS FALSE
    `the thing is currency including a currency note or coin which is legal tender in the country or territory in which it is issued` IS FALSE
    `the thing is a coin being metal used as money stamped and issued by or under the authority of the government of any country or territory in order to be so used` IS FALSE
    `forges or counterfeits or knowingly performs any part of the process of forging or counterfeiting the currency or bank note` IS FALSE
    `the currency or bank note is forged or counterfeit` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe the currency or bank note to be forged or counterfeit` IS FALSE
    `delivers or sells to or buys or receives from any other person or otherwise imports exports or traffics in or uses as genuine the currency or bank note` IS FALSE
    `has the currency or bank note in his possession` IS FALSE
    `intends to use the currency or bank note as genuine or that it may be used as genuine` IS FALSE
    `makes mends or performs any part of the process of making or mending or buys sells or disposes of or has in his possession any die machinery instrument or material` IS FALSE
    `the die machinery instrument or material is for the purpose of being used or he knows or has reason to believe that it is intended to be used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note` IS FALSE
    `the accused is within Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the thing abetted is the counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore` IS FALSE
    `performs on the coin an operation which diminishes its weight or alters its composition` IS FALSE
    `performs on the currency an operation which alters its appearance` IS FALSE
    `intends that the currency will pass as currency of a different description` IS FALSE
    `delivers to any other person as genuine or as currency of a different description from what it is or attempts to induce any person to receive as genuine or as currency of a different description the currency` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe that an operation mentioned in section 489F or 489G has been performed on the currency` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe that an offence under section 489F or 489G has been committed with respect to the currency` IS FALSE

`blank speech` MEANS Speech WITH
    `makes or publishes an imputation concerning any person` IS FALSE
    `by words spoken or intended to be read or by signs or visible representations` IS FALSE
    `intends to harm or knows or has reason to believe the imputation will harm that person reputation` IS FALSE
    `the imputation would lower that person moral or intellectual character in the estimation of others` IS FALSE
    `the imputation would lower that person character in respect of his calling in the estimation of others` IS FALSE
    `the imputation would lower that person credit in the estimation of others` IS FALSE
    `the imputation would cause it to be believed that the body of that person is in a loathsome or generally disgraceful state` IS FALSE
    `a section 499 exception applies` IS FALSE
    `threatens another with injury to person reputation or property` IS FALSE
    `or to the person or reputation of anyone in whom that person is interested` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause alarm` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause that person to do an act the person is not legally bound to do` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause that person to omit an act the person is legally entitled to do` IS FALSE
    `the intent is that the act or omission be the means of avoiding the execution of the threat` IS FALSE
    `the threat is to cause death or grievous hurt or destruction of property by fire` IS FALSE
    `intentionally insults and thereby gives provocation` IS FALSE
    `intending or knowing it likely the provocation will cause a breach of the public peace or any other offence` IS FALSE
    `makes publishes or circulates a statement rumour or report` IS FALSE
    `in written electronic or other media` IS FALSE
    `intent or likely to cause an officer or serviceman of the Singapore Armed Forces a visiting force or a section 140B person to mutiny or to disregard or fail in his duty` IS FALSE
    `intent or likely to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby a person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or public tranquillity` IS FALSE
    `intent or likely to incite any class or community to commit an offence against any other class or community` IS FALSE
    `has reasonable grounds for believing the statement is true and without the intents above` IS FALSE
    `prints or engraves any matter knowing or having good reason to believe that it is defamatory of any person` IS FALSE
    `sells or offers for sale any printed or engraved substance containing defamatory matter knowing that it contains such matter` IS FALSE
    `the threat is made by an anonymous communication or by a person who has taken precautions to conceal his name or abode` IS FALSE

`blank abetment` MEANS Abetment WITH
    `instigates any person to do the thing` IS FALSE
    `engages with one or more other persons in a conspiracy for the doing of the thing` IS FALSE
    `an act or illegal omission takes place in pursuance of that conspiracy and in order to the doing of that thing` IS FALSE
    `intentionally aids by any act or illegal omission the doing of the thing` IS FALSE
    `the thing would be an offence if committed by a person capable of committing an offence with the same intention or knowledge as the abettor` IS FALSE
    `the abetment takes place in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the act abetted would be committed outside Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the act abetted would constitute an offence if committed in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the offence abetted would be committed in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `any or all of the acts constituting the abetment were done outside Singapore` IS FALSE
    `facts unknown to the abettor make the doing of the thing impossible` IS FALSE
    `a different act from the act abetted was done` IS FALSE
    `the act done was a probable consequence of the abetment` IS FALSE
    `the act done was committed under the influence of the instigation or with the aid or in pursuance of the conspiracy which constituted the abetment` IS FALSE
    `the act was abetted with the intention on the part of the abettor of causing a particular effect` IS FALSE
    `an act for which the abettor is liable in consequence of the abetment causes a different effect from that intended` IS FALSE
    `the abettor knew that the act abetted was likely to cause that effect` IS FALSE
    `the abettor was present when the act or offence for which he would be punishable was committed` IS FALSE
    `the act abetted is committed in consequence of the abetment` IS FALSE
    `express provision is made by this Code or by any other written law for the punishment of the abetment` IS FALSE
    `the person abetted does the act with a different intention or knowledge from that of the abettor` IS FALSE
    `the act for which the abettor is liable under section 111 is committed in addition to the act abetted and constitutes a distinct offence` IS FALSE
    `the offence abetted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `the offence abetted is punishable with imprisonment` IS FALSE
    `abets the commission of an offence by the public generally or by any number or class of persons exceeding 10` IS FALSE
    `intends to facilitate or knows it to be likely that he will thereby facilitate the commission of an offence` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily conceals by any act or illegal omission the existence of a design to commit that offence or makes any representation which he knows to be false respecting that design` IS FALSE
    `the offence designed is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `the offence designed is punishable with imprisonment` IS FALSE
    `is a public servant whose duty as such it is to prevent the commission of the offence designed` IS FALSE
    `the offence designed is committed` IS FALSE

`blank conspiracy` MEANS Conspiracy WITH
    `the person` IS "Alice"
    `the other person` IS "Bob"
    `there is an agreement to commit or cause an offence` IS FALSE
    `the subject offence would be an offence if committed in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `location of the subject offence` IS `wholly in Singapore`
    `the other person intends to carry out the agreement` IS FALSE
    `facts unknown to the person make commission impossible` IS FALSE
    `any acts of the conspiracy were done in Singapore` IS FALSE

`blank attempt` MEANS Attempt WITH
    `intends to commit an offence punishable by this Code or any other written law` IS FALSE
    `takes a substantial step towards the commission of that offence` IS FALSE
    `the act is strongly corroborative of an intention to commit the offence` IS FALSE
    `facts unknown to the actor make the doing of the thing impossible` IS FALSE

`blank fault` MEANS Fault WITH
    `intends to cause wrongful gain to self or another` IS FALSE
    `intends to cause wrongful loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is of property to which the gainer is not legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is the avoidance of a loss of property which the avoider is not legally entitled to avoid` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is by unlawful means` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is of property to which the loser is legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is an exposure to the risk of a loss` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is by unlawful means` IS FALSE
    `the act is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `the actor knows the act is dishonest by those standards` IS FALSE
    `intends to deceive another person` IS FALSE
    `intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall by means of the deception` IS FALSE
    `the intended advantage or detriment is so slight that no reasonable person would complain` IS FALSE
    `does the act deliberately` IS FALSE
    `has sufficient cause to believe the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is aware that the relevant circumstance exists or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE
    `is wilfully blind to the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is done or believed without due care and attention` IS FALSE
    `intended to cause the effect by the means employed` IS FALSE
    `knew or had reason to believe the means employed were likely to cause the effect` IS FALSE
    `knows there is a real risk that the relevant circumstance exists or will exist` IS FALSE
    `knows there is a real risk that the effect will be caused` IS FALSE
    `it would have been unreasonable to have taken that risk` IS FALSE
    `omits to do an act which a reasonable person would do` IS FALSE
    `does an act which a reasonable person would not do` IS FALSE

`dishonest fault` MEANS Fault WITH
    `intends to cause wrongful gain to self or another` IS TRUE
    `intends to cause wrongful loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is of property to which the gainer is not legally entitled` IS TRUE
    `the intended gain is the avoidance of a loss of property which the avoider is not legally entitled to avoid` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is by unlawful means` IS TRUE
    `the intended loss is of property to which the loser is legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is an exposure to the risk of a loss` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is by unlawful means` IS FALSE
    `the act is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `the actor knows the act is dishonest by those standards` IS FALSE
    `intends to deceive another person` IS TRUE
    `intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall by means of the deception` IS TRUE
    `the intended advantage or detriment is so slight that no reasonable person would complain` IS FALSE
    `does the act deliberately` IS TRUE
    `has sufficient cause to believe the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is aware that the relevant circumstance exists or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE
    `is wilfully blind to the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is done or believed without due care and attention` IS FALSE
    `intended to cause the effect by the means employed` IS FALSE
    `knew or had reason to believe the means employed were likely to cause the effect` IS FALSE
    `knows there is a real risk that the relevant circumstance exists or will exist` IS FALSE
    `knows there is a real risk that the effect will be caused` IS FALSE
    `it would have been unreasonable to have taken that risk` IS FALSE
    `omits to do an act which a reasonable person would do` IS FALSE
    `does an act which a reasonable person would not do` IS FALSE

`blank homicide` MEANS Homicide WITH
    `causes death by doing an act` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of causing death` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to cause death` IS FALSE
    `the deceased was labouring under a disorder disease or bodily infirmity and the bodily injury accelerated the death` IS FALSE
    `the death might have been prevented by resorting to proper remedies and skilful treatment` IS FALSE
    `the death caused is that of a child in the mother womb` IS FALSE
    `any part of the child had been brought forth though the child may not have breathed or been completely born` IS FALSE
    `the act by which the death is caused is done with the intention of causing death` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as the offender knows to be likely to cause the death of the person to whom the harm is caused` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of causing bodily injury to any person and the bodily injury intended to be inflicted is sufficient in the ordinary course of nature to cause death` IS FALSE
    `knows that the act is so imminently dangerous that it must in all probability cause death or such bodily injury as is likely to cause death and commits it without any excuse for incurring the risk` IS FALSE
    `whilst deprived of the power of self-control by grave and sudden provocation causes the death of the person who gave the provocation or of any other person by mistake or accident` IS FALSE
    `an ordinary person of the same gender and age sharing such characteristics as would affect the gravity of the provocation and placed in the same situation would be deprived of self-control by it` IS FALSE
    `the provocation was sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for killing or doing harm to any person` IS FALSE
    `the offender knew or had reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of the powers of such public servant` IS FALSE
    `the provocation was given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence` IS FALSE
    `in the exercise of the right of private defence of person or property exceeds the power given by law and causes the death of the person against whom the right is exercised` IS FALSE
    `without premeditation as defined in the Explanation to Exception 2` IS FALSE
    `without any intention of doing more harm than is necessary for the purpose of such defence` IS FALSE
    `being a public servant or aiding a public servant acting for the advancement of public justice exceeds the powers given to him by law` IS FALSE
    `causes death by doing an act which he in good faith believes to be lawful and necessary for the due discharge of his duty as such public servant` IS FALSE
    `without ill will towards the person whose death is caused` IS FALSE
    `committed without premeditation in a sudden fight in the heat of passion upon a sudden quarrel` IS FALSE
    `without the offender having taken undue advantage or acted in a cruel or unusual manner` IS FALSE
    `the offender knew or had reason to believe that the person whose death was caused was acting in obedience to the law or was a public servant acting in the lawful exercise of the powers of such public servant` IS FALSE
    `the person whose death is caused being above 18 years of age suffers death or takes the risk of death with his own consent` IS FALSE
    `the offender being a woman voluntarily causes the death of her child being a child below 12 months of age` IS FALSE
    `at the time of the offence the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child or by reason of the effect of lactation consequent upon the birth` IS FALSE
    `at the time of the acts or omissions causing the death the offender was suffering from such abnormality of mind as substantially impaired his capacity to know the nature of those acts or omissions` IS FALSE
    `such abnormality of mind substantially impaired his capacity to know whether those acts or omissions are wrong` IS FALSE
    `such abnormality of mind substantially impaired his power to control his acts or omissions` IS FALSE
    `there was a substantial impairment of his capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `there was a substantial impairment of his capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `by doing anything which he intends or knows to be likely to cause death causes the death of a person whose death he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause` IS FALSE
    `causes the death of any person by doing a rash or negligent act not amounting to culpable homicide` IS FALSE
    `the victim is a child below 14 years of age a domestic worker or a vulnerable person` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a relevant person in relation to the victim within section 304B(2)` IS FALSE
    `causes the death of the victim by a course of conduct consisting of voluntarily causing hurt or knowingly causing neglect or both` IS FALSE
    `that course of conduct occurred on 2 or more occasions` IS FALSE
    `that course of conduct occurred on a single occasion and was protracted` IS FALSE
    `the victim dies as a result of the unlawful act of a person who was a member of the same household as the victim and had frequent contact with the victim` IS FALSE
    `the accused was a member of the same household as the victim and had frequent contact with the victim at the time of that act` IS FALSE
    `at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to the victim by the unlawful act of such a person` IS FALSE
    `the accused was the person whose act caused the victim death` IS FALSE
    `the accused was or ought to have been aware of that significant risk` IS FALSE
    `the accused failed to take such steps as could reasonably have been expected to protect the victim from that significant risk` IS FALSE
    `the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that the accused foresaw or ought to have foreseen` IS FALSE
    `the accused could not have been expected in the accused circumstances to take any such step` IS FALSE
    `abets the commission of the suicide or attempted suicide` IS FALSE
    `that person commits suicide` IS FALSE
    `that person attempts suicide` IS FALSE
    `the person who committed or attempted suicide is a minor below 18 years of age or a person who lacks capacity to understand the consequences of attempting or committing suicide` IS FALSE
    `knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person was such a minor or person who lacks capacity` IS FALSE
    `hurt is caused to any person in the course of the attempted suicide` IS FALSE
