§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 16, unborn children and infants`

-- ss 312 and 313.
#ASSERT `constitutes causing miscarriage` `a miscarriage caused without consent`
#ASSERT `constitutes causing miscarriage without consent` `a miscarriage caused without consent`
-- The "subject to the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974" opening takes the act out.
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes causing miscarriage` `a lawful termination`)
-- s 315 and the saving for the mother's life written into it.
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes child destruction` `a child destroyed to save the mother`)
#ASSERT `constitutes child destruction` `a child destroyed with no such necessity`
-- s 316, on its own Illustration.
#ASSERT `constitutes causing the death of a quick unborn child` `a quick unborn child killed`
-- s 317.
#ASSERT `constitutes exposure and abandonment of a child` `a child abandoned by its mother`

§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 16, kidnapping, abduction, slavery and forced labour`

-- s 361, and its Exception, and the "unless for an immoral or unlawful purpose" that
-- restores the section.
#ASSERT `the person kidnaps from lawful guardianship` `a child taken from its guardian`
#ASSERT `the person kidnaps` `a child taken from its guardian`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person kidnaps from lawful guardianship` `a father taking his own child in good faith`)
#ASSERT `the person kidnaps from lawful guardianship` `a father taking his own child for an unlawful purpose`
-- s 362: abduction is not a kind of kidnapping.
#ASSERT `the person abducts` `an adult deceived into going somewhere`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person kidnaps` `an adult deceived into going somewhere`)
#ASSERT `the person kidnaps or abducts` `an adult deceived into going somewhere`
-- s 364 builds on the abduction.
#ASSERT `constitutes kidnapping or abducting in order to murder` `an abduction in order to murder`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes kidnapping or abducting in order to murder` `an adult deceived into going somewhere`)
-- ss 370, 372 and 374.
#ASSERT `constitutes dealing in a person as a slave` `a person detained as a slave`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes habitual dealing in slaves` `a person detained as a slave`)
#ASSERT `constitutes selling a minor for prostitution` `a minor sold for prostitution`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes buying a minor for prostitution` `a minor sold for prostitution`)
#ASSERT `constitutes unlawful compulsory labour` `a worker compelled to labour`

§§ `Sexual offence context fixtures -- Chapter 16, sections 377C to 377D`

-- The blank context: no exploitative relationship, no misconception, no mistake as to age.
`no context facts` MEANS `Sexual Context` WITH
    `it is sexual because of its nature whatever its circumstances or any person purpose in relation to it` IS FALSE
    `it may be sexual because of its nature and is sexual because of its circumstances or the purpose of any person in relation to it or both` IS FALSE
    `the person is in circumstances in which the person has a reasonable expectation of privacy` IS FALSE
    `the person is in a state where the genital region buttocks or breasts if female are exposed or covered only in underwear` IS FALSE
    `the person is using a toilet showering or bathing` IS FALSE
    `the person is doing a sexual act that is not of a kind ordinarily done in public` IS FALSE
    `the court determines the relationship to be exploitative having regard to the age of the minor the age difference the nature of the relationship and the degree of control or influence` IS FALSE
    `the accused is the parent step-parent guardian or foster parent of the minor` IS FALSE
    `the accused is the de facto partner of the parent guardian or foster parent of the minor` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a member of the teaching or management staff of the school or educational institution at which the minor is a student` IS FALSE
    `the accused has an established personal relationship with the minor in connection with the provision of religious sporting musical or other instruction to the minor` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a custodial officer of an institution in which the minor is detained` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a registered medical practitioner a registered traditional Chinese medicine practitioner or a psychologist and the minor is a patient of the accused` IS FALSE
    `the accused is an advocate and solicitor or a counsellor and the minor is a client of the accused` IS FALSE
    `the contrary has been proved so that the presumption does not stand` IS FALSE
    `the accused is lawfully married to the minor` IS FALSE
    `the misconception is directly related to the nature of the act namely that it is not of a sexual nature` IS FALSE
    `the misconception is directly related to the purpose of the act namely that it is not for a sexual purpose` IS FALSE
    `the misconception is directly related to the identity of the person doing the act` IS FALSE
    `the person doing the act knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of such misconception` IS FALSE
    `the accused had a reasonable mistaken belief that the minor was of or above 18 years of age` IS FALSE
    `the fact that the minor is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age is a physical element of the offence` IS FALSE
    `the accused has previously been charged in court for an offence listed in section 377D(3)(a)` IS FALSE
    `the accused failed to take all reasonable steps to verify that the minor was of or above 18 years of age` IS FALSE
    `the other person is the spouse of the accused` IS FALSE
    `the spouse consented` IS FALSE

