§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 16, the sexual offence general provisions`

-- s 377CA(2): the presumption, its rebuttal, and the s 377CA(3) marriage carve-out.
#ASSERT `the relationship is exploitative of the minor` `a teacher of the minor`
#ASSERT NOT (`the relationship is exploitative of the minor` `a teacher of the minor, rebutted`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the relationship is exploitative of the minor` `a guardian lawfully married to the minor`)
-- s 377CB: the three misconceptions that vitiate, and Illustration (d) which does not.
#ASSERT `the consent is vitiated by misconception under section 377CB` `a misconception as to the nature of the act`
#ASSERT NOT (`the consent is vitiated by misconception under section 377CB` `a misconception as to the actor's attributes`)
-- s 377D: the defence, and its two defeaters, and its confinement to the 16-to-18 band.
#ASSERT `a mistake as to age is a defence` `a reasonable mistake that the minor was 18`
#ASSERT NOT (`a mistake as to age is a defence` `the same mistake by a person previously charged`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a mistake as to age is a defence` `a mistake where the victim was below 16`)

§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 16, sexual penetration`

-- s 375(1)(a) and the s 375(5) good-faith defence to it.
#ASSERT `constitutes rape` `penile penetration without consent` `no context facts`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes rape` `penile penetration with a good-faith belief in consent` `no context facts`)
-- s 375(1)(b): the good-faith belief is no answer to the below-14 limb.
#ASSERT `constitutes rape` `penile penetration of a person below 14` `no context facts`
-- s 375(4): but the spouse carve-out is.
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes rape` `penile penetration of a person below 14` `a consenting spouse`)
-- s 375(3): the aggravated form.
#ASSERT `the rape is in the section 375(3) aggravated form` `rape with hurt caused to facilitate it` `no context facts`
#ASSERT NOT (`the rape is in the section 375(3) aggravated form` `penile penetration without consent` `no context facts`)
-- s 376: the non-penile limb, which s 375 does not reach.
#ASSERT `constitutes sexual assault by penetration` `non-penile penetration without consent` `no context facts`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes rape` `non-penile penetration without consent` `no context facts`)
-- s 376A, and the s 376A(1A) displacement proviso.
#ASSERT `constitutes sexual penetration of a minor below 16` `penetration of a person below 16` `no context facts`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes sexual penetration of a minor below 16` `penetration of a person below 16 that is also rape` `no context facts`)
-- s 376AA needs the exploitative relationship, and yields to the s 377D defence.
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes exploitative sexual penetration of a minor` `exploitative penetration of a person of 17` `no context facts`)
#ASSERT `constitutes exploitative sexual penetration of a minor` `exploitative penetration of a person of 17` `an exploitative teacher relationship`
-- ss 376B and 376D.
#ASSERT `constitutes commercial sex with a minor` `commercial sex with a person below 18` `no context facts`
#ASSERT `constitutes organising a tour for commercial sex with a minor` `a tour organised for commercial sex abroad`
-- ss 376E and 376EA.
#ASSERT `constitutes sexual grooming of a minor below 16` `grooming a person below 16`
#ASSERT `constitutes exploitative sexual grooming of a minor` `grooming a person of 17 in an exploitative relationship` `an exploitative teacher relationship`
-- ss 376F and 376H: consent given, but procured.
#ASSERT `constitutes procurement of sexual activity with a person with mental disability` `procuring a consent from a person with mental disability`
#ASSERT `constitutes procurement of sexual activity by deception` `a deception about a protective measure`
-- s 376G.
#ASSERT `constitutes incest` `penetration of a sibling`
-- s 377: the causing limbs need the absence of that person's consent.
#ASSERT `constitutes sexual penetration of a corpse` `causing another to penetrate a corpse without consent`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes sexual penetration of a corpse` `causing another to penetrate a corpse with consent`)

§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 16, voyeurism, images and abuse material`

-- s 377BB(3), and the s 377BM(2) defence which answers it.
#ASSERT `constitutes voyeurism` `recording a person in a shower`
#ASSERT `constitutes voyeurism after defences` `recording a person in a shower`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes voyeurism after defences` `recording to report an offence`)
-- s 377BB(6) stands without the knowledge element.
#ASSERT `constitutes voyeurism` `installing a camera to enable voyeurism`
-- s 377BE(2): the threat limb, which no defence answers.
#ASSERT `constitutes threatening to distribute an intimate image` `threatening to distribute an intimate image`
-- s 377BK with the s 377BN(1) and s 377BN(3) defences.
#ASSERT `constitutes a child abuse material offence after defences` `possessing child abuse material deliberately`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes a child abuse material offence after defences` `possessing child abuse material inadvertently`)
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes a child abuse material offence after defences` `possessing child abuse material for research`)
-- s 377BG is answered by none of the s 377BN defences, which run to ss 377BH to 377BK.
#ASSERT `constitutes using a child in producing child abuse material` `using a child to produce such material`

§§ `Chapter 17 fixtures -- taking and trust`

-- s 380: theft committed in a building used as a human dwelling.
`a theft in a dwelling` MEANS `Property Taking` WITH
    `the property is movable` IS TRUE
    `intends to take the property out of the possession of any person` IS TRUE
    `without that person consent` IS TRUE
    `moves the property in order to such taking` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use` IS FALSE
    `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property` IS TRUE
    `the accused is a clerk or servant or employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing death hurt or restraint or fear of death hurt or restraint to any person in order to commit the theft or to effect escape after it or to retain property taken by it` IS FALSE
    `knows that the property was in the possession of a deceased person at the time of that person decease and has not since been in the possession of any person legally entitled to it` IS FALSE

-- s 378 alone, as the control for ss 380 to 382.
`a plain theft` MEANS `Property Taking` WITH
    `the property is movable` IS TRUE
    `intends to take the property out of the possession of any person` IS TRUE
    `without that person consent` IS TRUE
    `moves the property in order to such taking` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use` IS FALSE
    `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a clerk or servant or employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing death hurt or restraint or fear of death hurt or restraint to any person in order to commit the theft or to effect escape after it or to retain property taken by it` IS FALSE
    `knows that the property was in the possession of a deceased person at the time of that person decease and has not since been in the possession of any person legally entitled to it` IS FALSE

-- The Illustrations to s 382: a pistol carried in case the victim resists.
`a theft with a weapon prepared` MEANS `Property Taking` WITH
    `the property is movable` IS TRUE
    `intends to take the property out of the possession of any person` IS TRUE
    `without that person consent` IS TRUE
    `moves the property in order to such taking` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use` IS FALSE
    `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a clerk or servant or employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing death hurt or restraint or fear of death hurt or restraint to any person in order to commit the theft or to effect escape after it or to retain property taken by it` IS TRUE
    `knows that the property was in the possession of a deceased person at the time of that person decease and has not since been in the possession of any person legally entitled to it` IS FALSE

-- The Illustration to s 404: a servant takes the money before anyone entitled to it does.
`misappropriating a dead man's money` MEANS `Property Taking` WITH
    `the property is movable` IS TRUE
    `intends to take the property out of the possession of any person` IS FALSE
    `without that person consent` IS FALSE
    `moves the property in order to such taking` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use` IS TRUE
    `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a clerk or servant or employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing death hurt or restraint or fear of death hurt or restraint to any person in order to commit the theft or to effect escape after it or to retain property taken by it` IS FALSE
    `knows that the property was in the possession of a deceased person at the time of that person decease and has not since been in the possession of any person legally entitled to it` IS TRUE

-- s 409: entrustment in the way of a trade or business as a banker.
`a banker's breach of trust` MEANS Trust WITH
    `is entrusted with property or with any dominion over property` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts that property to own use` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly uses or disposes of that property in violation of a direction of law or legal contract touching the trust` IS FALSE
    `intentionally suffers any other person to do so` IS FALSE
    `the entrustment was of property for the purpose of transportation or storage for hire` IS FALSE
    `the accused is an employee or engaged in a capacity with the same fundamental qualities as an employee and was entrusted in that capacity` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in his capacity as a public servant` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in the way of his trade profession or business as a banker merchant factor broker attorney or agent` IS TRUE
    `the accused was entrusted in his professional capacity otherwise than by way of such a trade profession or business` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in his capacity as a director of a corporation an officer of an unincorporated association a partner in a partnership a key executive or a fiduciary` IS FALSE

-- s 405 alone, as the control for ss 407 to 409.
`a plain breach of trust` MEANS Trust WITH
    `is entrusted with property or with any dominion over property` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts that property to own use` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly uses or disposes of that property in violation of a direction of law or legal contract touching the trust` IS FALSE
    `intentionally suffers any other person to do so` IS FALSE
    `the entrustment was of property for the purpose of transportation or storage for hire` IS FALSE
    `the accused is an employee or engaged in a capacity with the same fundamental qualities as an employee and was entrusted in that capacity` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in his capacity as a public servant` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in the way of his trade profession or business as a banker merchant factor broker attorney or agent` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in his professional capacity otherwise than by way of such a trade profession or business` IS FALSE
    `the accused was entrusted in his capacity as a director of a corporation an officer of an unincorporated association a partner in a partnership a key executive or a fiduciary` IS FALSE

§§ `Chapter 17 fixtures -- extortion and robbery`

-- Illustration (c) to s 383: threatening to report an offence really committed. Extortion, because the harm may be caused legally or illegally.
`a threat to report a real offence` MEANS Extortion WITH
    `intentionally puts any person in fear of any harm to that person or to any other person in body mind reputation or property whether the harm is to be caused legally or illegally` IS TRUE
    `thereby dishonestly induces the person so put in fear to deliver to any person any property or valuable security or anything signed or sealed which may be converted into a valuable security` IS TRUE
    `in order to commit extortion puts or attempts to put any person in fear` IS FALSE
    `the fear is of death or of grievous hurt to that person or to any other` IS FALSE
    `the fear is of an accusation against that person or any other of having committed or attempted to commit an offence punishable with death with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 10 years` IS FALSE
    `the fear is of an accusation of having attempted to induce any other person to commit such an offence` IS FALSE

-- The fear was induced but no delivery followed, so s 383 is not made out -- but s 385 is.
`a threat that induced nothing` MEANS Extortion WITH
    `intentionally puts any person in fear of any harm to that person or to any other person in body mind reputation or property whether the harm is to be caused legally or illegally` IS TRUE
    `thereby dishonestly induces the person so put in fear to deliver to any person any property or valuable security or anything signed or sealed which may be converted into a valuable security` IS FALSE
    `in order to commit extortion puts or attempts to put any person in fear` IS TRUE
    `the fear is of death or of grievous hurt to that person or to any other` IS FALSE
    `the fear is of an accusation against that person or any other of having committed or attempted to commit an offence punishable with death with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 10 years` IS FALSE
    `the fear is of an accusation of having attempted to induce any other person to commit such an offence` IS FALSE

-- s 386: extortion committed by putting the victim in fear of grievous hurt.
`extortion by fear of grievous hurt` MEANS Extortion WITH
    `intentionally puts any person in fear of any harm to that person or to any other person in body mind reputation or property whether the harm is to be caused legally or illegally` IS TRUE
    `thereby dishonestly induces the person so put in fear to deliver to any person any property or valuable security or anything signed or sealed which may be converted into a valuable security` IS TRUE
    `in order to commit extortion puts or attempts to put any person in fear` IS FALSE
    `the fear is of death or of grievous hurt to that person or to any other` IS TRUE
    `the fear is of an accusation against that person or any other of having committed or attempted to commit an offence punishable with death with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 10 years` IS FALSE
    `the fear is of an accusation of having attempted to induce any other person to commit such an offence` IS FALSE

-- Illustration (a) to s 390(2): theft with wrongful restraint caused for that end.
`holding a man down and taking his money` MEANS Robbery WITH
    `in order to commit the theft or in committing it or in carrying away or attempting to carry away property obtained by it` IS TRUE
    `for that end voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to any person death hurt or wrongful restraint or fear of instant death instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint` IS TRUE
    `at the time of committing the extortion the offender is in the presence of the person put in fear` IS FALSE
    `commits the extortion by putting that person in fear of instant death instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint to that person or to some other person` IS FALSE
    `by so putting in fear induces the person then and there to deliver up the thing extorted` IS FALSE
    `5 or more persons conjointly commit or attempt to commit the robbery or the persons so committing or attempting together with those present and aiding amount to 5 or more` IS FALSE
    `attempts to commit robbery` IS FALSE
    `in committing or attempting to commit the robbery voluntarily causes hurt` IS FALSE
    `is jointly concerned in committing or attempting to commit the robbery` IS FALSE
    `one of the 5 or more persons conjointly committing the gang-robbery commits murder in so committing it` IS FALSE
    `at the time of committing or attempting to commit the robbery the offender is armed with or uses any deadly weapon` IS FALSE
    `at that time the offender causes grievous hurt to any person or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person` IS FALSE
    `makes any preparation for committing gang-robbery` IS FALSE
    `belongs to a gang of persons associated for the purpose of habitually committing gang-robbery` IS FALSE
    `belongs to a gang of persons associated for the purpose of habitually committing theft or robbery and not being gang-robbers` IS FALSE
    `is one of 5 or more persons assembled for the purpose of committing gang-robbery` IS FALSE

-- Illustration (b) to s 390(3): extortion in the victim's presence by fear of instant hurt, inducing delivery then and there.
`a pistol shown on the road` MEANS Robbery WITH
