§§ `Chapter 17 fixtures -- stolen property, deeds, mischief and trespass`

-- s 411: receiving property known to be stolen, with no reasonable excuse.
`receiving goods known to be stolen` MEANS `Stolen Property` WITH
    `the possession of the property has been transferred by theft extortion or robbery or the property has been criminally misappropriated or is property in respect of which criminal breach of trust or cheating has been committed` IS TRUE
    `the transfer misappropriation breach of trust or cheating was committed within or without Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the property has since come into the possession of a person legally entitled to the possession of it` IS FALSE
    `the property is property into or for which stolen property has been converted or exchanged or anything acquired by such conversion or exchange` IS FALSE
    `receives or retains the property` IS TRUE
    `habitually receives or deals in the property` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily assists in concealing or disposing of or making away with the property` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe the property to be stolen property or property obtained in whole or in part through an offence involving fraud or dishonesty` IS TRUE
    `knows or has reason to believe the possession of the property to have been transferred by the commission of gang-robbery` IS FALSE
    `receives the property from a person whom he knows or has reason to believe to belong or to have belonged to gang-robbers and knows or has reason to believe the property to have been stolen` IS FALSE
    `the accused proves a reasonable excuse to receive or retain the property and that he exercised reasonable care as soon as practicable after acquiring that knowledge or reason to believe` IS FALSE

-- The Illustration to s 412(2): the finder keeps the jewels safe and reports them promptly. The reasonable-excuse defence.
`keeping stolen jewels to report them` MEANS `Stolen Property` WITH
    `the possession of the property has been transferred by theft extortion or robbery or the property has been criminally misappropriated or is property in respect of which criminal breach of trust or cheating has been committed` IS TRUE
    `the transfer misappropriation breach of trust or cheating was committed within or without Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the property has since come into the possession of a person legally entitled to the possession of it` IS FALSE
    `the property is property into or for which stolen property has been converted or exchanged or anything acquired by such conversion or exchange` IS FALSE
    `receives or retains the property` IS TRUE
    `habitually receives or deals in the property` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily assists in concealing or disposing of or making away with the property` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe the property to be stolen property or property obtained in whole or in part through an offence involving fraud or dishonesty` IS TRUE
    `knows or has reason to believe the possession of the property to have been transferred by the commission of gang-robbery` IS FALSE
    `receives the property from a person whom he knows or has reason to believe to belong or to have belonged to gang-robbers and knows or has reason to believe the property to have been stolen` IS FALSE
    `the accused proves a reasonable excuse to receive or retain the property and that he exercised reasonable care as soon as practicable after acquiring that knowledge or reason to believe` IS TRUE

-- s 413, which has no reasonable-excuse defence -- so the same excuse does not answer it.
`habitually dealing in stolen goods` MEANS `Stolen Property` WITH
    `the possession of the property has been transferred by theft extortion or robbery or the property has been criminally misappropriated or is property in respect of which criminal breach of trust or cheating has been committed` IS FALSE
    `the transfer misappropriation breach of trust or cheating was committed within or without Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the property has since come into the possession of a person legally entitled to the possession of it` IS FALSE
    `the property is property into or for which stolen property has been converted or exchanged or anything acquired by such conversion or exchange` IS FALSE
    `receives or retains the property` IS FALSE
    `habitually receives or deals in the property` IS TRUE
    `voluntarily assists in concealing or disposing of or making away with the property` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe the property to be stolen property or property obtained in whole or in part through an offence involving fraud or dishonesty` IS TRUE
    `knows or has reason to believe the possession of the property to have been transferred by the commission of gang-robbery` IS FALSE
    `receives the property from a person whom he knows or has reason to believe to belong or to have belonged to gang-robbers and knows or has reason to believe the property to have been stolen` IS FALSE
    `the accused proves a reasonable excuse to receive or retain the property and that he exercised reasonable care as soon as practicable after acquiring that knowledge or reason to believe` IS TRUE

-- s 410: property ceases to be stolen property once a person legally entitled to it has possession.
`property recovered by its owner` MEANS `Stolen Property` WITH
    `the possession of the property has been transferred by theft extortion or robbery or the property has been criminally misappropriated or is property in respect of which criminal breach of trust or cheating has been committed` IS TRUE
    `the transfer misappropriation breach of trust or cheating was committed within or without Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the property has since come into the possession of a person legally entitled to the possession of it` IS TRUE
    `the property is property into or for which stolen property has been converted or exchanged or anything acquired by such conversion or exchange` IS FALSE
    `receives or retains the property` IS FALSE
    `habitually receives or deals in the property` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily assists in concealing or disposing of or making away with the property` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe the property to be stolen property or property obtained in whole or in part through an offence involving fraud or dishonesty` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe the possession of the property to have been transferred by the commission of gang-robbery` IS FALSE
    `receives the property from a person whom he knows or has reason to believe to belong or to have belonged to gang-robbers and knows or has reason to believe the property to have been stolen` IS FALSE
    `the accused proves a reasonable excuse to receive or retain the property and that he exercised reasonable care as soon as practicable after acquiring that knowledge or reason to believe` IS FALSE

-- s 421: a transfer without adequate consideration, intending to prevent distribution among creditors.
`transferring assets to defeat creditors` MEANS `Fraudulent Deed` WITH
    `dishonestly or fraudulently removes conceals or delivers to any person or transfers or causes to be transferred to any person without adequate consideration any property` IS TRUE
    `intending thereby to prevent or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby prevent the distribution of that property according to law among his creditors or the creditors of any other person` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly or fraudulently prevents any debt or demand due to himself or to any other person from being made available according to law for payment of his debts or the debts of that other person` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly or fraudulently signs executes or becomes a party to any deed or instrument which purports to transfer or subject to any charge any property or any interest in it` IS FALSE
    `the deed or instrument contains a false statement relating to the consideration for the transfer or charge or relating to the person for whose use or benefit it is really intended to operate` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly or fraudulently conceals or removes any property of himself or any other person or assists in the concealment or removal of it` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly releases any demand or claim to which he is entitled` IS FALSE

-- s 423: a deed of transfer containing a false statement of the consideration.
`a deed with a false consideration` MEANS `Fraudulent Deed` WITH
    `dishonestly or fraudulently removes conceals or delivers to any person or transfers or causes to be transferred to any person without adequate consideration any property` IS FALSE
    `intending thereby to prevent or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby prevent the distribution of that property according to law among his creditors or the creditors of any other person` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly or fraudulently prevents any debt or demand due to himself or to any other person from being made available according to law for payment of his debts or the debts of that other person` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly or fraudulently signs executes or becomes a party to any deed or instrument which purports to transfer or subject to any charge any property or any interest in it` IS TRUE
    `the deed or instrument contains a false statement relating to the consideration for the transfer or charge or relating to the person for whose use or benefit it is really intended to operate` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly or fraudulently conceals or removes any property of himself or any other person or assists in the concealment or removal of it` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly releases any demand or claim to which he is entitled` IS FALSE

-- s 425: destruction of property with intent to cause wrongful loss.
`smashing a neighbour's window` MEANS Mischief WITH
    `with intent to cause or knowing that he is likely to cause wrongful loss or damage to the public or any person` IS TRUE
    `causes the destruction of any property or such change in any property or in the situation of it as destroys or diminishes its value or utility or affects it injuriously` IS TRUE
    `the act causes or the accused knows it is likely to cause a disruption to the provision of any key service` IS FALSE
    `the act causes or the accused knows it is likely to cause a disruption to the performance of any duty or function of or the exercise of any power by the Government or a public agency` IS FALSE
    `commits the mischief by killing poisoning maiming or rendering useless any animal` IS FALSE
    `commits the mischief by fire or any explosive substance` IS FALSE
    `intending to cause or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause damage to any property` IS FALSE
    `intending to cause or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause the destruction of a building ordinarily used as a place of worship for the administration of justice for the transaction of public affairs for education or art for public use or ornament as a human dwelling or as a place for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `commits the mischief to any decked vessel or any vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards intending to destroy or render unsafe or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby destroy or render unsafe that vessel` IS FALSE
    `commits or attempts to commit that mischief to the vessel by fire or any explosive substance` IS FALSE
    `intentionally runs any vessel aground or ashore intending to commit theft of property contained in it or dishonestly to misappropriate any such property or with intent that such theft or misappropriation may be committed` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing to any person death hurt or wrongful restraint or fear of death hurt or wrongful restraint` IS FALSE

