    `the act causes or the accused knows it is likely to cause a disruption to the performance of any duty or function of or the exercise of any power by the Government or a public agency` IS FALSE
    `commits the mischief by killing poisoning maiming or rendering useless any animal` IS FALSE
    `commits the mischief by fire or any explosive substance` IS TRUE
    `intending to cause or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause damage to any property` IS FALSE
    `intending to cause or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause the destruction of a building ordinarily used as a place of worship for the administration of justice for the transaction of public affairs for education or art for public use or ornament as a human dwelling or as a place for the custody of property` IS TRUE
    `commits the mischief to any decked vessel or any vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards intending to destroy or render unsafe or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby destroy or render unsafe that vessel` IS FALSE
    `commits or attempts to commit that mischief to the vessel by fire or any explosive substance` IS FALSE
    `intentionally runs any vessel aground or ashore intending to commit theft of property contained in it or dishonestly to misappropriate any such property or with intent that such theft or misappropriation may be committed` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing to any person death hurt or wrongful restraint or fear of death hurt or wrongful restraint` IS FALSE

-- s 439, which requires no mischief at all -- only the running aground and the intent.
`running a ship aground to loot it` MEANS Mischief WITH
    `with intent to cause or knowing that he is likely to cause wrongful loss or damage to the public or any person` IS FALSE
    `causes the destruction of any property or such change in any property or in the situation of it as destroys or diminishes its value or utility or affects it injuriously` IS FALSE
    `the act causes or the accused knows it is likely to cause a disruption to the provision of any key service` IS FALSE
    `the act causes or the accused knows it is likely to cause a disruption to the performance of any duty or function of or the exercise of any power by the Government or a public agency` IS FALSE
    `commits the mischief by killing poisoning maiming or rendering useless any animal` IS FALSE
    `commits the mischief by fire or any explosive substance` IS FALSE
    `intending to cause or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause damage to any property` IS FALSE
