    `having made preparation for causing to any person death hurt or wrongful restraint or fear of death hurt or wrongful restraint` IS FALSE

-- s 441: entry on another's property with intent to annoy the person in possession.
`entering land to annoy the occupier` MEANS Trespass WITH
    `enters into or upon property in the possession of another` IS TRUE
    `having lawfully entered into or upon such property unlawfully remains there` IS FALSE
    `with intent to commit an offence` IS FALSE
    `with intent to intimidate insult or annoy any person in possession of the property` IS TRUE
    `the property entered or remained in is a building tent container or vessel used as a human dwelling or a building used as a place for worship or as a place for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with death` IS FALSE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing hurt to any person for assaulting any person for wrongfully restraining any person or for putting any person in fear of hurt assault or wrongful restraint` IS FALSE
    `is found armed with any instrument for shooting stabbing or cutting or any instrument which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death without lawful authority or a lawful purpose` IS FALSE
    `is found having his face covered or otherwise disguised with intent to commit any offence` IS FALSE
    `is found equipped with any article or instrument for use in the course of or in connection with any house-breaking` IS FALSE
    `while committing the house-breaking causes grievous hurt to any person or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person` IS FALSE
    `at the time of the house-breaking a person guilty of it voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person` IS FALSE
    `is jointly concerned in committing the house-breaking` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly or with intent to commit mischief breaks open or unfastens any closed receptacle which contains or which he believes to contain property` IS FALSE
    `is entrusted with that closed receptacle without having authority to open it` IS FALSE

-- s 442: criminal trespass into a building used as a human dwelling -- house-breaking.
`entering a house to steal` MEANS Trespass WITH
    `enters into or upon property in the possession of another` IS TRUE
    `having lawfully entered into or upon such property unlawfully remains there` IS FALSE
    `with intent to commit an offence` IS TRUE
    `with intent to intimidate insult or annoy any person in possession of the property` IS FALSE
    `the property entered or remained in is a building tent container or vessel used as a human dwelling or a building used as a place for worship or as a place for the custody of property` IS TRUE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with death` IS FALSE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing hurt to any person for assaulting any person for wrongfully restraining any person or for putting any person in fear of hurt assault or wrongful restraint` IS FALSE
    `is found armed with any instrument for shooting stabbing or cutting or any instrument which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death without lawful authority or a lawful purpose` IS FALSE
    `is found having his face covered or otherwise disguised with intent to commit any offence` IS FALSE
    `is found equipped with any article or instrument for use in the course of or in connection with any house-breaking` IS FALSE
    `while committing the house-breaking causes grievous hurt to any person or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person` IS FALSE
    `at the time of the house-breaking a person guilty of it voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person` IS FALSE
    `is jointly concerned in committing the house-breaking` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly or with intent to commit mischief breaks open or unfastens any closed receptacle which contains or which he believes to contain property` IS FALSE
    `is entrusted with that closed receptacle without having authority to open it` IS FALSE

-- Entry into a dwelling without either s 441 intent. Not criminal trespass, so not house-breaking either.
`entering a house with no intent` MEANS Trespass WITH
    `enters into or upon property in the possession of another` IS TRUE
    `having lawfully entered into or upon such property unlawfully remains there` IS FALSE
    `with intent to commit an offence` IS FALSE
    `with intent to intimidate insult or annoy any person in possession of the property` IS FALSE
    `the property entered or remained in is a building tent container or vessel used as a human dwelling or a building used as a place for worship or as a place for the custody of property` IS TRUE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with death` IS FALSE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing hurt to any person for assaulting any person for wrongfully restraining any person or for putting any person in fear of hurt assault or wrongful restraint` IS FALSE
    `is found armed with any instrument for shooting stabbing or cutting or any instrument which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death without lawful authority or a lawful purpose` IS FALSE
    `is found having his face covered or otherwise disguised with intent to commit any offence` IS FALSE
    `is found equipped with any article or instrument for use in the course of or in connection with any house-breaking` IS FALSE
    `while committing the house-breaking causes grievous hurt to any person or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person` IS FALSE
    `at the time of the house-breaking a person guilty of it voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person` IS FALSE
    `is jointly concerned in committing the house-breaking` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly or with intent to commit mischief breaks open or unfastens any closed receptacle which contains or which he believes to contain property` IS FALSE
    `is entrusted with that closed receptacle without having authority to open it` IS FALSE

-- s 453(1)(c): being found equipped for house-breaking. No trespass is required.
`being found with a jemmy` MEANS Trespass WITH
    `enters into or upon property in the possession of another` IS FALSE
    `having lawfully entered into or upon such property unlawfully remains there` IS FALSE
    `with intent to commit an offence` IS FALSE
    `with intent to intimidate insult or annoy any person in possession of the property` IS FALSE
    `the property entered or remained in is a building tent container or vessel used as a human dwelling or a building used as a place for worship or as a place for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with death` IS FALSE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing hurt to any person for assaulting any person for wrongfully restraining any person or for putting any person in fear of hurt assault or wrongful restraint` IS FALSE
    `is found armed with any instrument for shooting stabbing or cutting or any instrument which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death without lawful authority or a lawful purpose` IS FALSE
    `is found having his face covered or otherwise disguised with intent to commit any offence` IS FALSE
    `is found equipped with any article or instrument for use in the course of or in connection with any house-breaking` IS TRUE
    `while committing the house-breaking causes grievous hurt to any person or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person` IS FALSE
    `at the time of the house-breaking a person guilty of it voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person` IS FALSE
    `is jointly concerned in committing the house-breaking` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly or with intent to commit mischief breaks open or unfastens any closed receptacle which contains or which he believes to contain property` IS FALSE
    `is entrusted with that closed receptacle without having authority to open it` IS FALSE

§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 17, aggravated theft, extortion and robbery`

-- ss 380 and 382 build on s 378, and the plain theft is the control.
#ASSERT `constitutes theft in a dwelling house` `a theft in a dwelling` `dishonest fault`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes theft in a dwelling house` `a plain theft` `dishonest fault`)
#ASSERT `constitutes theft after preparation for causing hurt` `a theft with a weapon prepared` `dishonest fault`
-- s 404, on its own Illustration.
#ASSERT `constitutes misappropriation of a deceased person property` `misappropriating a dead man's money` `dishonest fault`
-- ss 407 to 409 build on s 405.
#ASSERT `constitutes criminal breach of trust in a special capacity` `a banker's breach of trust` `dishonest fault`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes criminal breach of trust in a special capacity` `a plain breach of trust` `dishonest fault`)
-- s 383 needs the delivery; without it the case is s 385 only.
#ASSERT `constitutes extortion` `a threat to report a real offence`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes extortion` `a threat that induced nothing`)
#ASSERT `constitutes putting in fear to commit extortion` `a threat that induced nothing`
#ASSERT `constitutes extortion by fear of death or grievous hurt` `extortion by fear of grievous hurt`
-- s 390(2) and s 390(3): the two routes into robbery, on Illustrations (a) and (b).
#ASSERT `constitutes robbery` `holding a man down and taking his money` `a plain theft` `a threat to report a real offence` `dishonest fault`
#ASSERT `constitutes robbery` `a pistol shown on the road` `blank property taking` `a threat to report a real offence` `dishonest fault`
-- Illustration (d): extortion, but not robbery -- no presence and no fear of instant harm.
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes robbery` `a child held by the gang elsewhere` `blank property taking` `a threat to report a real offence` `dishonest fault`)
#ASSERT `constitutes extortion` `a threat to report a real offence`
-- ss 391 and 397.
#ASSERT `constitutes gang-robbery` `five men robbing together` `a plain theft` `a threat to report a real offence` `dishonest fault`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes gang-robbery` `holding a man down and taking his money` `a plain theft` `a threat to report a real offence` `dishonest fault`)
#ASSERT `constitutes armed or deadly robbery` `an armed robbery` `a plain theft` `a threat to report a real offence` `dishonest fault`
-- s 401 needs no robbery at all.
#ASSERT `constitutes belonging to a gang of thieves` `belonging to a gang of thieves`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes belonging to a gang of gang-robbers` `belonging to a gang of thieves`)

§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 17, stolen property, fraudulent deeds, mischief and trespass`

-- s 411 and the s 411(3) reasonable-excuse defence, on the s 412(2) Illustration.
#ASSERT `constitutes receiving stolen property` `receiving goods known to be stolen`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes receiving stolen property` `keeping stolen jewels to report them`)
-- s 413 has no such defence, so the same excuse does not answer it.
#ASSERT `constitutes habitually dealing in stolen property` `habitually dealing in stolen goods`
-- s 410: property recovered by a person entitled to it ceases to be stolen property.
#ASSERT `the property is stolen property` `receiving goods known to be stolen`
#ASSERT NOT (`the property is stolen property` `property recovered by its owner`)
-- ss 421 and 423.
#ASSERT `constitutes fraudulent removal to defeat creditors` `transferring assets to defeat creditors`
#ASSERT `constitutes fraudulent execution of a deed` `a deed with a false consideration`
-- ss 425, 436 and 439.
#ASSERT `constitutes mischief` `smashing a neighbour's window`
#ASSERT `constitutes mischief by fire to destroy a building` `setting fire to a dwelling`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes mischief by fire to destroy a building` `smashing a neighbour's window`)
-- s 439 requires no mischief.
#ASSERT `constitutes running a vessel aground to commit theft` `running a ship aground to loot it`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes mischief` `running a ship aground to loot it`)
-- ss 441 and 442: house-breaking is criminal trespass into a dwelling, so the intent is needed.
#ASSERT `constitutes criminal trespass` `entering land to annoy the occupier`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes house-breaking` `entering land to annoy the occupier`)
#ASSERT `constitutes house-breaking` `entering a house to steal`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes criminal trespass` `entering a house with no intent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes house-breaking` `entering a house with no intent`)
-- s 453 requires no trespass.
#ASSERT `constitutes going equipped for house-breaking` `being found with a jemmy`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes criminal trespass` `being found with a jemmy`)

§§ `Chapter 18 fixtures -- forged documents, false instruments and accounts`

-- Illustration (a) to s 464: A adds a cypher to Z's letter of credit on B, to defraud B. With `dishonest fault` this is s 463 forgery, and the base for ss 466 to 469.
`altering a letter of credit` MEANS `Document Making` WITH
    `makes a document or electronic record or part of one` IS TRUE
    `makes signs seals executes or affixes an electronic signature` IS FALSE
    `intends it to be believed that it was made signed sealed executed or affixed by or by the authority of a person by whom the actor knows it was not` IS FALSE
    `without lawful authority alters a document or electronic record in any material part` IS TRUE
    `causes a person who does not know the contents to sign seal execute or alter` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person` IS FALSE
    `intent to support any claim or title` IS FALSE
    `intent to cause any person to part with property` IS TRUE
    `intent to cause any person to enter into any express or implied contract` IS FALSE
    `intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed` IS TRUE

-- s 467: the document forged purports to be a will.
`a forged will` MEANS `Forged Document` WITH
    `the document or electronic record purports to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice or a register of birth baptism marriage or burial or a register kept by a public servant as such or a certificate document or electronic record purporting to be made by a public servant in his official capacity or an authority to institute or defend a suit or to take any proceedings in it or to confess judgment or a power of attorney` IS FALSE
    `the document purports to be a valuable security or a will or an authority to adopt a child or purports to give authority to any person to make or transfer any valuable security or to receive the principal interest or dividends on it or to receive or deliver any money movable property or valuable security or purports to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money or the delivery of any movable property or valuable security` IS TRUE
    `intends that the document or electronic record forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating` IS FALSE
    `intends that the document or electronic record forged shall harm the reputation of any person or knows that it is likely to be used for that purpose` IS FALSE
    `the document or electronic record is a false document or false electronic record made wholly or in part by forgery` IS FALSE
    `uses as genuine a document or electronic record` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe the document or electronic record to be a forged document or forged electronic record` IS FALSE
    `has in his possession a document or electronic record knowing it to be forged` IS FALSE
    `intends that the document or electronic record shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine` IS FALSE
    `makes or counterfeits any seal plate or other instrument for making an impression` IS FALSE
    `has in his possession any such seal plate or other instrument knowing it to be counterfeit` IS FALSE
    `intends that the seal plate or instrument shall be used for the purpose of committing a forgery which would be punishable under section 467` IS FALSE
    `intends that the seal plate or instrument shall be used for the purpose of committing a forgery which would be punishable under a section of Chapter 18 other than section 467` IS FALSE
    `makes or has in his custody or under his control a machine or implement or paper or other material` IS FALSE
    `to his knowledge the machine implement paper or material is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any false instrument` IS FALSE
    `the machine implement paper or material is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any instrument` IS FALSE
    `intends that he or another person makes a false instrument using the machine implement paper or material in order to induce another person to accept it as genuine or to induce a machine to respond to it as if it were a genuine instrument` IS FALSE
    `intends that by reason of so accepting it the person induced does or does not do some act` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in a person permanently or temporarily losing property including by not getting what he might get` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in a person being deprived of an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in a person being deprived of an opportunity to gain a financial advantage otherwise than by way of remuneration` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in somebody being given an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration from a person` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in somebody being given an opportunity to gain a financial advantage from a person otherwise than by way of remuneration` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced will be the result of a person having accepted a false instrument as genuine in connection with his performance of any duty` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission intended to be induced is one induced by a machine responding to the instrument as if it were genuine` IS FALSE
    `the act intended to be induced is one the person has an enforceable duty to do or the omission intended to be induced is of an act the person is not entitled to do` IS FALSE
    `counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating a document or electronic record` IS FALSE
    `has in his possession any material upon or in the substance of which any such device or mark has been counterfeited` IS FALSE
    `intends that the device or mark shall be used for the purpose of giving the appearance of authenticity to any document or electronic record then forged or thereafter to be forged on that material` IS FALSE
    `the device or mark is used for the purpose of authenticating a document described in section 467` IS FALSE
    `cancels destroys or defaces or attempts to cancel destroy or deface or secretes or attempts to secrete a document or commits mischief in respect of it` IS FALSE
    `the document is or purports to be a will or an authority to adopt a child or any valuable security` IS FALSE
    `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person` IS FALSE
    `is a clerk officer or servant or is employed or acting in the capacity of a clerk officer or servant` IS FALSE
    `intentionally and with intent to defraud destroys alters conceals mutilates or falsifies any book electronic record paper writing valuable security or account or a set of them which belongs to or is in the possession of his employer or has been received by him for or on behalf of his employer` IS FALSE
    `intentionally and with intent to defraud makes or abets the making of any false entry in or omits or alters or abets the omission or alteration of any material particular from or in any such book electronic record paper writing valuable security or account or set of them` IS FALSE

