§§ `Chapter 8 fixtures -- unlawful assembly`
-- s 141(c) and s 142: a member of an unlawful assembly.
`joining a crowd bent on breaking into a warehouse` MEANS `Unlawful Assembly` WITH
    `the assembly is of 5 or more persons` IS TRUE
    `the common object is to overawe by criminal force or show of criminal force the Legislative or Executive Government or any public servant in the exercise of his lawful power` IS FALSE
    `the common object is to resist the execution of any law or of any legal process` IS FALSE
    `the common object is to commit any offence` IS TRUE
    `the common object is by criminal force or show of criminal force to any person to take or obtain possession of property or to deprive any person of the enjoyment of a right of way or of the use of water or other incorporeal right in his possession or enjoyment or to enforce any right or supposed right` IS FALSE
    `the common object is by criminal force or show of criminal force to compel any person to do what he is not legally bound to do or to omit to do what he is legally entitled to do` IS FALSE
    `is aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly` IS TRUE
    `intentionally joins the assembly or continues in it` IS TRUE
    `is armed with a deadly weapon or with anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `joins or continues in the assembly` IS FALSE
    `knows that the unlawful assembly has been commanded in the manner prescribed by law to disperse` IS FALSE
    `the assembly is of 5 or more persons likely to cause a disturbance of the public peace` IS FALSE
    `the assembly has been lawfully commanded to disperse and the person knowingly joins or continues in it after the command` IS FALSE
    `force or violence is used by the assembly or by any member of it in prosecution of the common object` IS FALSE
    `an offence is committed by a member of the assembly in prosecution of the common object or such as the members knew to be likely to be committed in prosecution of that object` IS FALSE
    `is a member of the same assembly at the time that offence is committed` IS FALSE
    `hires engages employs or promotes or connives at the hiring engagement or employment of any person to join or become a member of the unlawful assembly` IS FALSE
    `assaults or threatens to assault or obstructs or attempts to obstruct a public servant in the discharge of his duty in endeavouring to disperse an unlawful assembly or to suppress a riot or an affray or uses or threatens or attempts to use criminal force to such public servant` IS FALSE
    `intentionally or rashly by doing anything which is illegal gives provocation to any person` IS FALSE
    `intends or knows it to be likely that the provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed` IS FALSE
    `the offence of rioting is committed in consequence of the provocation` IS FALSE
    `an unlawful assembly is held or a riot is committed on land` IS FALSE
    `is the owner or occupier of the land or has or claims an interest in it` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager knows that the offence is being or has been committed or has reason to believe it is likely to be committed` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager gives the earliest notice in his power to the principal officer at the nearest police station` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager having reason to believe the offence is about to be committed uses all lawful means in his power to prevent it` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager in the event of the offence taking place uses all lawful means in his power to disperse or suppress it` IS FALSE
    `a riot is committed for the benefit or on behalf of a person who is the owner or occupier of land respecting which the riot takes place or who claims an interest in the land or in the subject of the dispute which gave rise to the riot or who has accepted or derived any benefit from it` IS FALSE
    `is that person` IS FALSE
    `is the agent or manager of that person` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager has reason to believe that the riot was likely to be committed or that the unlawful assembly by which it was committed was likely to be held` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager uses all lawful means in his power to prevent the riot or assembly from taking place and to suppress and disperse it` IS FALSE
    `harbours receives or assembles in a house or premises in his occupation or charge or under his control persons knowing that they have been or are about to be hired engaged or employed to join or become members of an unlawful assembly` IS FALSE
    `intends to permit or facilitate them joining or becoming members of an unlawful assembly or to screen them or any of them from punishment` IS FALSE
    `is engaged or hired or offers or attempts to be hired or engaged to do or assist in doing any of the acts specified in section 141` IS FALSE
    `being so engaged or hired goes armed or engages or offers to go armed with a deadly weapon or with anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death` IS FALSE
-- s 141 needs 5 or more persons.
