    `intends or knows it to be likely that the provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed` IS FALSE
    `the offence of rioting is committed in consequence of the provocation` IS FALSE
    `an unlawful assembly is held or a riot is committed on land` IS FALSE
    `is the owner or occupier of the land or has or claims an interest in it` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager knows that the offence is being or has been committed or has reason to believe it is likely to be committed` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager gives the earliest notice in his power to the principal officer at the nearest police station` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager having reason to believe the offence is about to be committed uses all lawful means in his power to prevent it` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager in the event of the offence taking place uses all lawful means in his power to disperse or suppress it` IS FALSE
    `a riot is committed for the benefit or on behalf of a person who is the owner or occupier of land respecting which the riot takes place or who claims an interest in the land or in the subject of the dispute which gave rise to the riot or who has accepted or derived any benefit from it` IS FALSE
    `is that person` IS FALSE
    `is the agent or manager of that person` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager has reason to believe that the riot was likely to be committed or that the unlawful assembly by which it was committed was likely to be held` IS FALSE
    `he or his agent or manager uses all lawful means in his power to prevent the riot or assembly from taking place and to suppress and disperse it` IS FALSE
    `harbours receives or assembles in a house or premises in his occupation or charge or under his control persons knowing that they have been or are about to be hired engaged or employed to join or become members of an unlawful assembly` IS FALSE
    `intends to permit or facilitate them joining or becoming members of an unlawful assembly or to screen them or any of them from punishment` IS FALSE
    `is engaged or hired or offers or attempts to be hired or engaged to do or assist in doing any of the acts specified in section 141` IS TRUE
    `being so engaged or hired goes armed or engages or offers to go armed with a deadly weapon or with anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death` IS FALSE
§§ `Chapter 9 fixtures -- offences by or relating to public servants`
-- s 161 Illustration (a): a judge obtains a situation for his brother as a reward for deciding a cause.
`a judge taking a job for his brother as a reward` MEANS `Public Servant Offence` WITH
    `is a public servant` IS TRUE
    `expects to be a public servant` IS FALSE
    `accepts or obtains or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain from any person for himself or for any other person any gratification whatever` IS TRUE
    `the gratification is other than legal remuneration` IS TRUE
    `as a motive or reward for doing or forbearing to do any official act or for showing or forbearing to show in the exercise of his official functions favour or disfavour to any person or for rendering or attempting to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet or with any public servant as such` IS TRUE
    `as a motive or reward for inducing by corrupt or illegal means any public servant to do or forbear to do any official act or in the exercise of his official functions to show favour or disfavour to any person or to render or attempt to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet or with any public servant as such` IS FALSE
    `as a motive or reward for inducing by the exercise of personal influence any public servant to do or forbear to do any official act or in the exercise of his official functions to show favour or disfavour to any person or to render or attempt to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet or with any public servant as such` IS FALSE
    `is the public servant in respect of whom an offence under section 162 or 163 is committed` IS FALSE
    `abets that offence` IS FALSE
    `accepts or obtains or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain for himself or for any other person any valuable thing without consideration or for a consideration which he knows to be inadequate` IS FALSE
    `from a person whom he knows to have been or to be or to be likely to be concerned in any proceedings or business transacted or about to be transacted by him or having any connection with his official functions or those of any public servant to whom he is subordinate or from a person whom he knows to be interested in or related to the person so concerned` IS FALSE
    `knowingly disobeys a direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as a public servant` IS FALSE
    `intends to cause or knows it to be likely that he will by the disobedience cause injury to any person` IS FALSE
    `is charged as a public servant with the preparation or translation of a document or electronic record` IS FALSE
    `frames or translates the document or electronic record in a manner which he knows or believes to be incorrect` IS FALSE
    `intends thereby to cause or knows it to be likely that he may thereby cause injury to any person` IS FALSE
    `is legally bound as a public servant not to engage in trade` IS FALSE
    `engages in trade` IS FALSE
    `is legally bound as a public servant not to purchase or bid for certain property` IS FALSE
    `purchases or bids for that property in his own name or in the name of another or jointly or in shares with others` IS FALSE
    `pretends to hold a particular office as a public servant knowing that he does not hold it or falsely personates another person holding such office` IS FALSE
    `in that assumed character does or attempts to do any act under colour of the office` IS FALSE
    `does not belong to a certain class of public servants` IS FALSE
    `wears any garb or carries any token resembling any garb or token used by that class of public servants` IS FALSE
    `intends that it may be believed or knows it to be likely to be believed that he belongs to that class of public servants` IS FALSE
