    `intends thereby to cause or knows it to be likely that he will thereby cause the public servant to use his lawful power to the injury or annoyance of any person or to do or omit anything which he ought not to or would not do or omit if the true state of facts were known to him` IS FALSE
    `offers resistance to the taking of property by the lawful authority of a public servant knowing or having reason to believe that the person is such public servant` IS FALSE
    `intentionally obstructs a sale of property offered for sale by the lawful authority of a public servant as such` IS FALSE
    `at a sale of property held by the lawful authority of a public servant as such purchases or bids for property on account of himself or another person whom he knows to be under a legal incapacity to purchase that property at that sale` IS FALSE
    `at such a sale bids for property not intending to perform the obligations under which he lays himself by the bidding` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily obstructs a public servant in the discharge of his public functions` IS FALSE
    `is bound by law to render or furnish assistance to a public servant in the execution of his public duty` IS FALSE
    `intentionally omits to give that assistance` IS FALSE
    `the assistance was demanded by a public servant legally competent to demand it for executing a process lawfully issued by a court or preventing the commission of an offence or suppressing a riot or an affray or apprehending a person charged with or guilty of an offence or escaped from lawful custody` IS FALSE
    `knows that by an order promulgated by a public servant lawfully empowered to promulgate it he is directed to abstain from a certain act or to take certain order with certain property in his possession or under his management` IS FALSE
    `disobeys that direction` IS FALSE
    `the disobedience causes or tends to cause obstruction annoyance or injury or risk of obstruction annoyance or injury to any person lawfully employed` IS FALSE
    `the disobedience causes or tends to cause danger to human life health or safety or causes or tends to cause a riot or an affray` IS FALSE
    `holds out a threat of injury to a public servant or to a person in whom he believes that public servant to be interested` IS TRUE
    `for the purpose of inducing the public servant to do any act or to forbear or delay to do any act connected with the exercise of his public functions` IS TRUE
    `holds out a threat of injury to any person` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of inducing that person to refrain or desist from making a legal application for protection against any injury to a public servant legally empowered as such to give or cause such protection` IS FALSE
-- s 190.
`threatening a neighbour not to go to the police` MEANS `Contempt Of Authority` WITH
    `the person is an individual` IS FALSE
    `absconds in order to avoid being arrested on a warrant or served with a summons notice or order proceeding from a public servant legally competent as such to issue it` IS FALSE
    `the summons notice order or proclamation is to attend in person or by agent before a court or to produce a document or electronic record before a court` IS FALSE
