§§ `Chapter 11 fixtures -- false evidence`
-- s 191 Illustration (a) and s 193: false evidence in a judicial proceeding.
`swearing falsely to an admission at trial` MEANS `False Evidence` WITH
    `is legally bound by an oath or by an express provision of law to state the truth or is bound by law to make a declaration upon any subject` IS TRUE
    `makes a statement verbally or otherwise which is false and which he knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true` IS TRUE
    `causes a circumstance to exist or makes a false entry in a book record or electronic record or makes a document or electronic record containing a false statement` IS FALSE
    `intends that the circumstance false entry or false statement may appear in evidence in a judicial proceeding or in a proceeding taken by law before a public servant as such or before an arbitrator` IS FALSE
    `intends that it so appearing may cause a person who in that proceeding is to form an opinion upon the evidence to entertain an erroneous opinion touching a point material to the result of the proceeding` IS FALSE
    `the false evidence is given or fabricated intentionally` IS TRUE
    `the false evidence is given in or fabricated for use in a stage of a judicial proceeding including a trial before a court martial and an investigation directed by law preliminary to or directed by a court of justice` IS TRUE
    `intends thereby to cause or knows it to be likely that he will thereby cause a person to be convicted of an offence which is capital` IS FALSE
    `an innocent person is convicted and executed in consequence of the false evidence` IS FALSE
    `intends thereby to cause or knows it to be likely that he will thereby cause a person to be convicted of an offence which is not capital but punishable with imprisonment for 7 years or upwards` IS FALSE
    `the offence of which conviction is intended is punishable with imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `corruptly uses or attempts to use as true or genuine evidence any evidence which he knows to be false or fabricated` IS FALSE
    `issues or signs a certificate required by law to be given or signed or relating to a fact of which such certificate is by law admissible in evidence` IS FALSE
    `knows or believes that the certificate is false in a material point` IS FALSE
    `corruptly uses or attempts to use such a certificate as a true certificate knowing it to be false in a material point` IS FALSE
    `makes or subscribes a declaration which a court of justice or a public servant or other person is bound or authorised by law to receive as evidence of any fact` IS FALSE
    `in the declaration makes a statement which is false and which he knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true touching a point material to the object for which the declaration is made or used` IS FALSE
    `corruptly uses or attempts to use as true such a declaration knowing it to be false in a material point` IS FALSE
-- s 191 Illustration (c): a true statement of belief is not false evidence.
