§§ `Chapter 11 fixtures -- offences against public justice`
-- s 201 Illustration.
`helping a murderer hide the body` MEANS `Public Justice` WITH
    `the offence concerned is punishable with death` IS TRUE
    `the offence concerned is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe that an offence has been committed` IS TRUE
    `causes evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear` IS TRUE
    `intends to screen the offender from legal punishment` IS TRUE
    `gives information respecting that offence which he knows or believes to be false` IS FALSE
    `intentionally omits to give information respecting that offence which he is legally bound to give` IS FALSE
    `secretes or destroys a document or electronic record which he may be lawfully compelled to produce as evidence before a court of justice or in a proceeding lawfully held before a public servant as such or obliterates or renders illegible the whole or any part of it` IS FALSE
    `intends to prevent the document or electronic record from being produced or used as evidence before that court or public servant or does so after having been lawfully summoned or required to produce it for that purpose` IS FALSE
    `does an act that has a tendency to obstruct prevent pervert or defeat the course of justice` IS FALSE
    `being sentenced to imprisonment leaves or attempts to leave Singapore unlawfully to avoid serving the sentence` IS FALSE
    `the act is a mere warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted for perjury if he gives false evidence` IS FALSE
    `knows that the act is likely to obstruct prevent pervert or defeat the course of justice` IS FALSE
    `intends to obstruct prevent pervert or defeat the course of justice` IS FALSE
    `gives confers or procures or promises or offers to give confer or procure or attempts to procure any gratification to upon or for any person upon an agreement or understanding that a person aware of an offence which any person is legally bound to give information respecting will abstain from reporting it to the police or an agency charged by law with investigating offences` IS FALSE
    `gives confers or procures or promises or offers to give confer or procure or attempts to procure any gratification to upon or for any person upon an agreement or understanding that a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding will give false testimony or withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence` IS FALSE
    `attempts by any means to induce a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding to give false testimony or withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence` IS FALSE
    `asks receives or obtains or agrees or attempts to receive or obtain any property or benefit for himself or any other person upon an agreement or understanding that a person will as a witness in a judicial proceeding give false testimony or withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence` IS FALSE
    `falsely personates another` IS FALSE
    `in that assumed character makes an admission or statement or confesses judgment or causes process to be issued or becomes bail or security or does any other act in a suit or criminal prosecution` IS FALSE
    `removes conceals transfers or delivers to any person any property or interest in property` IS FALSE
    `accepts receives or claims any property or interest in property knowing that he has no right or rightful claim to it or practises any deception touching any right to property or an interest in property` IS FALSE
    `intends thereby to prevent the property or interest from being taken as a forfeiture or in satisfaction of a fine under a sentence pronounced or which he knows to be likely to be pronounced by a court of justice or other competent authority or from being taken in execution of a decree or order or under or pursuant to an enforcement order made or which he knows to be likely to be made by a court of justice in a civil suit` IS FALSE
    `causes or suffers a decree or order to be passed against him at the suit of any person for a sum not due or for a larger sum than is due or for property or an interest in property to which that person is not entitled or causes or suffers a decree or order to be executed or enforced against him after it has been satisfied or for anything in respect of which it has been satisfied` IS FALSE
    `obtains a decree or order against any person for a sum not due or for a larger sum than is due or for property or an interest in property to which he is not entitled or causes a decree or order to be executed or enforced against any person after it has been satisfied or for anything in respect of which it has been satisfied or suffers or permits any such act to be done in his name` IS FALSE
    `intends to cause injury to a person` IS FALSE
    `institutes or causes to be instituted a criminal proceeding against that person or falsely charges that person with having committed an offence` IS FALSE
    `knows that there is no just or lawful ground for the proceeding or charge against that person` IS FALSE
    `the criminal proceeding is instituted on a false charge of an offence punishable with death or with imprisonment for 7 years or upwards` IS FALSE
    `an offence has been committed` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe that the person is the offender` IS FALSE
    `harbours or conceals that person` IS FALSE
    `accepts or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain any gratification for himself or any other person or any restitution of property to himself or any other person` IS FALSE
    `in consideration of his concealing an offence or of his screening a person from legal punishment for an offence or of his not proceeding against a person for the purpose of bringing him to legal punishment` IS FALSE
    `gives or causes or offers or agrees to give or cause any gratification to any person or to restore or cause the restoration of any property to any person` IS FALSE
    `in consideration of that person concealing an offence or screening a person from legal punishment for an offence or not proceeding against a person for the purpose of bringing him to legal punishment` IS FALSE
    `the offence may lawfully be compounded` IS FALSE
    `takes or agrees or consents to take any gratification for himself or any other person under pretence or on account of helping a person to recover movable property of which he has been deprived by an offence punishable under this Code` IS FALSE
    `uses all means in his power to cause the offender to be apprehended and convicted of the offence` IS FALSE
    `a person convicted of or charged with an offence and in lawful custody for it has escaped from that custody or a public servant in the exercise of his lawful powers has ordered a person to be apprehended for an offence` IS FALSE
    `knows of the escape or of the order for apprehension` IS FALSE
    `intends to prevent that person from being apprehended` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe that persons are about to commit or have recently committed robbery or gang-robbery` IS FALSE
    `harbours those persons or any of them` IS FALSE
    `intends to facilitate the commission of the robbery or gang-robbery or to screen those persons or any of them from punishment` IS FALSE
    `supplies the person with shelter food drink money clothes arms ammunition or means of conveyance or assists the person in any way to evade apprehension` IS FALSE
    `is a public servant` IS FALSE
    `knowingly disobeys a direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as a public servant` IS FALSE
    `intends thereby to save or knows it to be likely that he will thereby save a person from legal punishment or subject him to a lesser punishment than that to which he is liable or intends to save or knows that he is likely thereby to save property from forfeiture or a charge to which it is liable by law` IS FALSE
    `is charged as a public servant with the preparation of a record or other writing` IS FALSE
    `frames the record or writing in a manner which he knows to be incorrect` IS FALSE
    `intends to cause or knows it to be likely that he will thereby cause loss or injury to the public or to any person or intends thereby to save or knows it to be likely that he will thereby save a person from legal punishment or intends to save or knows that he is likely thereby to save property from forfeiture or other charge to which it is liable by law` IS FALSE
    `corruptly or with intent to cause injury to any person makes or pronounces in any stage of a judicial proceeding a report order verdict or decision which he knows to be contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `is in an office that gives him legal authority to commit persons for trial or to confinement or to keep persons in confinement` IS FALSE
    `corruptly or with intent to cause injury to any person commits a person for trial or to confinement or keeps a person in confinement in the exercise of that authority` IS FALSE
    `knows that in doing so he is acting contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `is legally bound as a public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement a person charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence` IS FALSE
    `is legally bound as a public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement a person under sentence of a court of justice for an offence or lawfully committed to custody` IS FALSE
    `intentionally omits to apprehend that person or intentionally suffers that person to escape or intentionally aids that person in escaping or attempting to escape from confinement` IS FALSE
    `is legally bound as a public servant to keep in confinement a person charged with or convicted of an offence or lawfully committed to custody` IS FALSE
    `negligently suffers that person to escape from confinement` IS FALSE
    `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to his own lawful apprehension for an offence with which he is charged or of which he has been convicted or escapes or attempts to escape from custody in which he is lawfully detained for such an offence` IS FALSE
    `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person for an offence or rescues or attempts to rescue another person from custody in which that person is lawfully detained for an offence` IS FALSE
    `is legally bound as a public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement a person in a case not provided for in section 221 222 or 223 or in any other law for the time being in force` IS FALSE
    `intentionally or negligently omits to apprehend that person or suffers him to escape from confinement` IS FALSE
    `in a case not provided for in section 224 or 225 or in any other law for the time being in force intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself or of another person or escapes or attempts to escape from custody in which he is lawfully detained or rescues or attempts to rescue another person from custody in which that person is lawfully detained` IS FALSE
    `does anything which by a law in force in Singapore he is prohibited from doing or omits to do anything which he is so enjoined to do` IS FALSE
    `no special punishment is provided by the law for the commission or omission` IS FALSE
    `intentionally offers insult or causes interruption to a public servant while sitting in any stage of a judicial proceeding or conducting a mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process under written law` IS FALSE
    `by personation or otherwise intentionally causes or knowingly suffers himself to be returned empanelled or sworn as an assessor in a case in which he knows that he is not entitled by law to be so returned empanelled or sworn` IS FALSE
    `knowing himself to have been returned empanelled or sworn as an assessor contrary to law voluntarily serves as such assessor` IS FALSE
-- s 201 second limb, and s 203.
