§§ `Chapter 12 fixtures -- Government stamps`
-- s 25: intends to deceive, and an advantage or detriment by the deception, not too slight.
`fraudulent fault` MEANS Fault WITH
    `intends to cause wrongful gain to self or another` IS FALSE
    `intends to cause wrongful loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is of property to which the gainer is not legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is the avoidance of a loss of property which the avoider is not legally entitled to avoid` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is by unlawful means` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is of property to which the loser is legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is an exposure to the risk of a loss` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is by unlawful means` IS FALSE
    `the act is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `the actor knows the act is dishonest by those standards` IS FALSE
    `intends to deceive another person` IS TRUE
    `intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall by means of the deception` IS TRUE
    `the intended advantage or detriment is so slight that no reasonable person would complain` IS FALSE
    `does the act deliberately` IS FALSE
    `has sufficient cause to believe the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is aware that the relevant circumstance exists or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE
    `is wilfully blind to the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is done or believed without due care and attention` IS FALSE
    `intended to cause the effect by the means employed` IS FALSE
    `knew or had reason to believe the means employed were likely to cause the effect` IS FALSE
    `knows there is a real risk that the relevant circumstance exists or will exist` IS FALSE
    `knows there is a real risk that the effect will be caused` IS FALSE
    `it would have been unreasonable to have taken that risk` IS FALSE
    `omits to do an act which a reasonable person would do` IS FALSE
    `does an act which a reasonable person would not do` IS FALSE
-- s 255.
`printing fake revenue stamps` MEANS `Government Stamp` WITH
    `the stamp is a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue` IS TRUE
    `the stamp is a stamp certificate issued under the Stamp Duties Act 1929` IS FALSE
    `counterfeits or knowingly performs any part of the process of counterfeiting the stamp` IS TRUE
    `causes a genuine stamp of one denomination to appear like a genuine stamp of a different denomination` IS FALSE
    `has in his possession any instrument or material for the purpose of being used or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used for counterfeiting the stamp` IS FALSE
    `makes performs any part of the process of making buys sells or disposes of any instrument for the purpose of being used or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used for counterfeiting the stamp` IS FALSE
    `sells or offers for sale a stamp which he knows or has reason to believe to be a counterfeit of the stamp` IS FALSE
    `has in his possession a stamp which he knows to be a counterfeit of the stamp` IS FALSE
    `intends to use or dispose of the counterfeit as a genuine stamp or in order that it may be used as a genuine stamp` IS FALSE
    `uses as genuine a stamp knowing it to be a counterfeit of the stamp` IS FALSE
    `intends to cause loss to the Government` IS FALSE
    `removes or effaces from a substance bearing the stamp any writing or document for which the stamp has been used or removes from a writing or document a stamp which has been used for it in order that the stamp may be used for a different writing or document` IS FALSE
    `uses for any purpose the stamp which he knows to have been before used` IS FALSE
    `erases or removes from the stamp a mark put or impressed on it to denote that it has been used or knowingly has in his possession or sells or disposes of a stamp from which such a mark has been erased or removed or sells or disposes of a stamp which he knows to have been used` IS FALSE
-- s 255 Explanation.
