§§ `Chapter 14 fixtures -- public tranquility`
-- s 267A.
`a street brawl` MEANS `Public Nuisance` WITH
    `two or more persons disturb the public peace by fighting in a public place and the person is one of them` IS TRUE
    `utters words or makes a sign or visible representation or places before a person an object or posts publishes distributes sells or offers for sale a document or communicates an electronic record` IS FALSE
    `makes prints or otherwise reproduces imports possesses or has under his control such a document for the purpose of posting publishing distributing selling or offering it for sale or makes such an electronic record for the purpose of communicating it` IS FALSE
    `the words sign representation object document or electronic record contains an incitement to violence or counsels disobedience to the law or to a lawful order of a public servant or is likely to lead to a breach of the peace` IS FALSE
    `intends violence disobedience to the law or such lawful order or breach of the peace to occur` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe that violence disobedience to the law or such lawful order or breach of the peace is likely to occur as a result` IS FALSE
    `intends violence disobedience to the law or such lawful order or breach of the peace to occur by the carrying out of that purpose` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe that violence disobedience to the law or such lawful order or breach of the peace is likely to occur by the carrying out of that purpose` IS FALSE
    `does an act or is guilty of an illegal omission` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission causes common injury danger or annoyance to the public or to the people in general who dwell or occupy property in the vicinity` IS FALSE
