§§ `Chapter 14 fixtures -- public health and safety`
-- s 269.
`carelessly breaking quarantine while infectious` MEANS `Public Health And Safety` WITH
    `does an act which is and which he knows or has reason to believe to be likely to spread the infection of a disease dangerous to life` IS TRUE
    `the act is done unlawfully or negligently` IS TRUE
    `the act is done intentionally or rashly` IS FALSE
    `knowingly disobeys a rule lawfully made and promulgated for putting a vessel into a state of quarantine or for regulating the intercourse of vessels in quarantine with the shore or with other vessels or for regulating the intercourse between places where an infectious disease prevails and other places` IS FALSE
    `adulterates an article of food or drink so as to make it noxious as food or drink` IS FALSE
    `intends to sell the article as food or drink or knows it to be likely that it will be sold as food or drink` IS FALSE
    `sells or offers or exposes for sale as food or drink an article which has been rendered or has become noxious or is in a state unfit for food or drink` IS FALSE
    `knows or has reason to believe that the article is noxious as food or drink` IS FALSE
    `adulterates a drug or medical preparation so as to lessen its efficacy or change its operation or make it noxious` IS FALSE
    `intends that the drug or medical preparation be sold or used for or knows it to be likely that it will be sold or used for a medicinal purpose as if it had not undergone the adulteration` IS FALSE
    `knows a drug or medical preparation to have been adulterated so as to lessen its efficacy change its operation or render it noxious` IS FALSE
    `sells the adulterated drug or offers or exposes it for sale or issues it from a dispensary for medicinal purposes as unadulterated or causes it to be used for medicinal purposes by a person not knowing of the adulteration` IS FALSE
    `knowingly sells or offers or exposes for sale or issues from a dispensary for medicinal purposes a drug or medical preparation as a different drug or medical preparation` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily corrupts or fouls the water of a public spring or reservoir so as to render it less fit for the purpose for which it is ordinarily used` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily vitiates the atmosphere in any place so as to make it noxious to the health of persons in general dwelling or carrying on business in the neighbourhood or passing along a public way` IS FALSE
    `drives a vehicle or rides on a public way in a manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person` IS FALSE
    `navigates a vessel in a manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person` IS FALSE
    `exhibits a false light mark or buoy` IS FALSE
    `intends or knows it to be likely that the exhibition will mislead a navigator` IS FALSE
    `knowingly or negligently conveys or causes to be conveyed for hire a person by water in a vessel which is in such a state or so loaded as to endanger the life of that person` IS FALSE
    `by doing an act or by omitting to take order with property in his possession or under his charge causes danger obstruction or injury to a person in a public way or public line of navigation` IS FALSE
    `does with a dangerous or harmful substance including fire or anything likely to cause fire an act so rashly or negligently or omits to take such measure with such a substance in his possession as is sufficient to guard against probable danger to human life grievous hurt or hurt from it` IS FALSE
    `with fire or anything likely to cause fire rashly or negligently causes or substantially contributes to the risk of causing a fire` IS FALSE
    `a fire occurs` IS FALSE
    `deposits drops places or throws a cigarette or part of one a cigar a match stick charcoal incense embers or anything likely to cause fire in a place and a fire occurs at that place or in its vicinity within 60 minutes of that act` IS FALSE
    `the contrary of the section 286 presumption is proved` IS FALSE
    `does with machinery in his possession or under his care an act so rashly or negligently or omits to take such measure with such machinery as is sufficient to guard against probable danger to human life grievous hurt or hurt from it` IS FALSE
    `in pulling down or repairing a building knowingly or negligently omits to take such measure as is sufficient to guard against probable danger to human life from the fall of the building or any part of it` IS FALSE
    `knowingly or negligently omits to take such measure with an animal as is sufficient to guard against probable danger to human life or probable danger of grievous hurt from the animal` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission is likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission endangers human life` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission is likely to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `the fire causes damage to or diminishes the value or utility of property belonging to any other person or the Government` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission causes hurt or injury to any other person` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission causes grievous hurt to any other person` IS FALSE
    `the act or omission causes the death of any other person` IS FALSE
