§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 5, sections 109 to 120, and Chapters 6 to 15`

-- ss 109, 115 and 116 split on whether the act abetted is committed, and all yield to an express provision.
#ASSERT `section 109 applies to the abetment` `instigating a bribe that is accepted`
#ASSERT NOT (`section 109 applies to the abetment` `instigating a bribe that is refused`)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 109 applies to the abetment` `an abetment with its own express punishment`)
#ASSERT `section 116 applies to the abetment` `instigating a bribe that is refused`
#ASSERT NOT (`section 116 applies to the abetment` `instigating a bribe that is accepted`)
#ASSERT `section 115 applies to the abetment` `instigating a murder that is not committed`
#ASSERT NOT (`section 116 applies to the abetment` `instigating a murder that is not committed`)
#ASSERT (`the section 115 punishment of the abettor` `instigating a murder that is not committed`)'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`the section 109 punishment of the abettor` `instigating a bribe that is accepted` (`imprisonment up to or fine or both` 3))'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`the section 109 punishment of the abettor` `instigating a bribe that is refused` (`imprisonment up to or fine or both` 3))'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 0
-- s 116(2): the minimum does not bind the abettor.
#ASSERT (`the section 116 punishment of the abettor` `instigating a bribe that is refused` (`imprisonment from to and caning of not less than strokes` 2 7 6))'s `minimum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the section 116 punishment of the abettor` `instigating a bribe that is refused` (`imprisonment from to and caning of not less than strokes` 2 7 6))'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `section 110 applies to the abetment` `abetting with a different intention from the doer`
#ASSERT `the abettor is liable to cumulative punishment under section 112` `instigating resistance to a distress that causes grievous hurt`
#ASSERT NOT (`the abettor is liable to cumulative punishment under section 112` `instigating a bribe that is accepted`)
#ASSERT `constitutes abetting an offence by the public or by more than 10 persons` `a placard instigating more than 10 workers`
-- ss 118 to 120: the concealment shape, and the punishments.
#ASSERT `constitutes concealing a design to commit a capital or life offence` `misdirecting the police from a gang-robbery`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment` `misdirecting the police from a gang-robbery`)
#ASSERT (`the section 118 punishment` `misdirecting the police from a gang-robbery`)'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `constitutes a public servant concealing a design to commit an offence he must prevent` `a police officer sitting on a robbery design`
#ASSERT (`the section 119 punishment` `a police officer sitting on a robbery design` (`imprisonment up to or fine or both` 10))'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `constitutes concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment` `concealing a design to commit theft`
#ASSERT (`the section 120 punishment` `concealing a design to commit theft` (`imprisonment up to or fine or both` 8))'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment` `an innocent silence about a design`)
-- Chapter 6.
#ASSERT `constitutes waging war against the Government` `joining an insurrection`
#ASSERT `constitutes an offence against the President` `plotting to imprison the President`
#ASSERT `constitutes an offence against authority` `plotting to depose the President`
#ASSERT `constitutes abetting an offence against the President or authority` `abetting a plot against the President`
#ASSERT `constitutes omitting to inform of an offence against the State` `keeping silent about a plot one must report`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes omitting to inform of an offence against the State` `knowing of a plot with no duty to report`)
#ASSERT `constitutes preparing to wage war against the Government` `stockpiling arms for an uprising`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes preparing to wage war against the Government` `stockpiling arms for a collection`)
#ASSERT `constitutes concealing a design to wage war` `hiding a war plan to help it along`
#ASSERT `constitutes assaulting or overawing the President or a Member` `blockading a Minister to force a decision`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes assaulting or overawing the President or a Member` `assaulting a Minister over a parking space`)
#ASSERT `constitutes waging war against a friendly power` `raiding a neighbouring friendly state`
#ASSERT `constitutes depredation on a friendly power` `looting across a friendly border`
#ASSERT `constitutes receiving property taken by war or depredation` `fencing the loot of a border raid`
#ASSERT `constitutes voluntarily allowing a prisoner of State or war to escape` `a warder letting a prisoner of war walk out`
#ASSERT `constitutes negligently suffering a prisoner of State or war to escape` `a warder dozing while a prisoner of war walks out`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes voluntarily allowing a prisoner of State or war to escape` `a warder dozing while a prisoner of war walks out`)
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes voluntarily allowing a prisoner of State or war to escape` `a civilian letting a prisoner of war walk out`)
#ASSERT `constitutes aiding rescuing or harbouring a prisoner of State or war` `sheltering an escaped prisoner of war`
#ASSERT `constitutes aiding rescuing or harbouring a prisoner of State or war` `feeding a parolee who has overstepped his limits`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes aiding rescuing or harbouring a prisoner of State or war` `sheltering a prisoner of war still in custody`)
#ASSERT `constitutes aiding rescuing or harbouring a prisoner of State or war` `blocking the recapture of a prisoner of war`
#ASSERT `a Chapter 6 offence is made out` `joining an insurrection`
#ASSERT NOT (`a Chapter 6 offence is made out` `blank state offence`)
-- Chapters 6A and 6B.
#ASSERT `constitutes piracy by the law of nations` `boarding a ship on the high seas`
#ASSERT NOT (`the piracy attracts the section 130B(2) capital punishment` `boarding a ship on the high seas`)
#ASSERT `the piracy attracts the section 130B(2) capital punishment` `boarding a ship and shooting the crew`
#ASSERT `constitutes a piratical act` `stealing a Singapore ship`
#ASSERT `constitutes a piratical act` `inciting a mutiny on a Singapore ship`
#ASSERT `constitutes genocide` `killing members of a group to destroy it`
#ASSERT `constitutes genocide` `preventing births in a group to destroy it`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes genocide` `preventing births without the intent to destroy`)
#ASSERT (`the punishment for genocide` `killing members of a group to destroy it`)'s `death is mandatory`
#ASSERT NOT ((`the punishment for genocide` `preventing births in a group to destroy it`)'s `death is available`)
#ASSERT (`the punishment for genocide` `preventing births in a group to destroy it`)'s `imprisonment for life is available`
-- Chapter 7.
#ASSERT `constitutes abetting mutiny or seducing from duty` `urging a soldier to mutiny`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes abetting a mutiny that is committed` `urging a soldier to mutiny`)
#ASSERT `constitutes abetting a mutiny that is committed` `urging a soldier to mutiny and the mutiny follows`
#ASSERT `constitutes abetting mutiny or seducing from duty` `urging a police officer to mutiny`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes abetting mutiny or seducing from duty` `urging a security guard to mutiny`)
#ASSERT `constitutes abetting mutiny or seducing from duty` `tempting a soldier from his post`
#ASSERT `constitutes abetting an assault on a superior officer` `urging a soldier to strike his sergeant`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes abetting an assault on a superior officer that is committed` `urging a soldier to strike his sergeant`)
#ASSERT `constitutes abetting an assault on a superior officer that is committed` `urging a soldier to strike his sergeant and he does`
#ASSERT `constitutes abetting desertion` `urging a soldier to desert`
#ASSERT `constitutes harbouring a deserter` `hiding a deserter from the military police`
