#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes effacing writing or removing a used stamp` `washing a stamped deed to reuse the stamp with no intent` `blank fault`)
-- The s 25 route: a fraudulent Fault carries s 261 without the intent-to-cause-loss fact.
#ASSERT `constitutes effacing writing or removing a used stamp` `washing a stamped deed to reuse the stamp with no intent` `fraudulent fault`
#ASSERT `constitutes reusing a Government stamp` `reusing a stamp known to be used` `blank fault`
#ASSERT `constitutes erasing the mark of a used Government stamp` `rubbing out the cancellation mark` `blank fault`
-- s 255(2): the stamp certificate extension reaches ss 255 to 262 and not s 263.
#ASSERT `constitutes counterfeiting a Government stamp` `counterfeiting a stamp certificate`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes erasing the mark of a used Government stamp` `rubbing out the cancellation mark on a stamp certificate` `blank fault`)
