§§ `Assertions -- the screen over Chapters 6 to 15`

-- s 4A is now computed from the Chapter 6 and 6B tests as well as asserted.
#ASSERT `the act is deemed committed in Singapore under section 4A on the encoded tests` `a citizen joining an insurrection abroad`
#ASSERT `Singapore has territorial reach over the proposed act` `a citizen joining an insurrection abroad`
#ASSERT NOT (`the act is deemed committed in Singapore under section 4A on the encoded tests` `a foreigner joining an insurrection abroad`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Singapore has territorial reach over the proposed act` `a foreigner joining an insurrection abroad`)
#ASSERT `the proposed act constitutes an offence of war against the Government` `a citizen joining an insurrection abroad`
-- Schedule items 1 and 2 are now classified from the s 268A to 268C tests.
#ASSERT `the conduct is a specified offence in the Schedule` `a bomb hoax in Singapore`
#ASSERT `the proposed act constitutes a hoax of a harmful thing` `a bomb hoax in Singapore`
#ASSERT NOT (`the conduct is a specified offence in the Schedule` `innocent act in Singapore`)
-- s 139 closes the Chapter 7 wrapper for a person subject to service discipline law.
#ASSERT NOT (`the proposed act constitutes an armed forces offence` `a soldier urging mutiny under service law`)
#ASSERT `the proposed act constitutes an armed forces offence` `a civilian urging mutiny`
-- s 6 runs over the new chapters as over the old.
#ASSERT NOT (`the proposed act constitutes affray or incitement` `a street brawl by a child of 8`)
#ASSERT `a general exception applies` `a street brawl by a child of 8`
#ASSERT `the proposed act constitutes giving or fabricating false evidence` `perjury in Singapore`
#ASSERT `any screened offence is indicated` `perjury in Singapore`
#ASSERT `the proposed act constitutes a reused Government stamp offence` `washing a stamp to reuse it fraudulently`
#ASSERT NOT (`any screened offence is indicated` `innocent act in Singapore`)

#EVAL `the offence screen of` `perjury in Singapore`
